  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: KTlY-lHs_Ew (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KTlY-lHs_Ew)<SEP>YouTube Video: Mr1cjAz2y9I (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mr1cjAz2y9I)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and some conflicting or repetitive points.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The entity in question is \"Action.\" The contaminated text has several points. The first point mentions a process to identify and name one's current emotion. The second describes Action as reactive behaviors driven by external circumstances, contrasting with intentionality. The third talks about Action being dualistic with \"considered\" and \"inclusive\" aspects. The fourth point is just a repetition that Action is correctly written, which seems like filler.

The challenge is integrating these points into a coherent summary. The first point might be a separate process, but the instructions say to include all aspects. However, the user wants only the spiritual teaching. The process of identifying emotions might be part of a broader concept related to Action. The second and third points clearly define Action in a spiritual context. The repetition about correct spelling is irrelevant.

So, the clean summary should mention the process as part of Action's context, then the reactive behaviors, and the dualistic nature. Need to present this in 1-4 sentences, plain English, no markdown. Avoid any developer notes. Make sure it's cohesive and starts with the entity name.
</think>

Action is a term associated with reactive behaviors driven by external circumstances, contrasting with intentionality and emotional presence in relationships. It is characterized by a dualistic nature, encompassing \"considered\" and \"inclusive\" aspects, reflecting a paradoxical relationship between intentionality and inclusivity in human behavior. The term also appears in contexts referencing a process to identify and name one's current emotion, though this connection remains implicit.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
