<urn:mukthiguru:Aham%20Brahmasmi> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Aham Brahmasmi";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779665702"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6aebd99b80a116244470eacf183c4202<SEP>chunk-61c0437442c1a79367c1612c9b022b8f<SEP>chunk-82784ea8fabb1f9041b72681c23fac84<SEP>chunk-c2e9ff77673d9126b2f975a8e07b2ddc<SEP>chunk-11324ba4a521604eab0a83749fcd1adc";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Aham Brahmasmi is a Sanskrit phrase that functions as a mantra and chant, central to Soul Sync practices and meditation. It is interpreted as meaning “I am the limitless consciousness” and is used to align the practitioner’s self with universal consciousness. The phrase is also recognized as a classical Advaita Vedanta statement, where it conveys the unity of self and universal consciousness, often rendered as “I am Brahman.”

Despite textual ambiguities, including an unclear original phrase “Ahamra, Massmen,” the phrase is considered a likely intended expression and is sometimes presented as a philosophical phrase replacing the unclear wording to fit the spiritual context. The phrase thus serves both as a meditative tool and a philosophical declaration of non‑dual identity.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: M_BYTcsLQuY (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M_BYTcsLQuY)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

