<urn:mukthiguru:Akam%20Ketra> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Akam Ketra is a term corrected from “Akan Ketra” in the source text, indicating the accurate term used. It is described as a powerful vortex of universal energy that facilitates Kundalini awakening during meditation by channeling energy into the crown chakra, pulling up the sleeping Kundalini.  

Akam Ketra also functions as a mystic powerhouse symbolizing divine energy and unity, representing a spiritual or philosophical entity within the discussed framework. In Kundalini yoga, Akam Ketra refers to a mystical energy center or powerhouse, emphasizing inner unity and self-realization as a spiritual principle or practice.<SEP>Akam Ketra is described as a mystic powerhouse linked to divine experiences in spiritual contexts.<SEP>Akam Ketra is a mystic powerhouse associated with divine experiences and spiritual awakening.<SEP>A mystic powerhouse representing the divine center within the self, central to the Limitless Field meditation.<SEP>Akam Ketra is described as a \"mystic powerhouse\" within the meditation context.<SEP>Akam Ketra is described as a mystic powerhouse or sacred space within the spiritual framework of the meditation practice.<SEP>Akam Ketra is described as a mystic powerhouse associated with divine meditation and the chanting of the Akam Mantra.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UrVvSqKYU8c)";
