  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-fd88fca76d8bbe7034dd353f047d1281<SEP>chunk-bfc222041dab5af4f8a47b40b1c47cc5<SEP>chunk-5a061c3e192c4aaa5026aa79274bb0f1<SEP>chunk-7ac9109abdb5bdc9de2685e960e358c1<SEP>chunk-98219edafe8ffc379bb20679c2f8f076<SEP>chunk-86b06c28798f4c4a7bd03b34bd895d71<SEP>chunk-b4ef0432d09dd625d180cc94f3e0ef2e<SEP>chunk-f11387cad436a638d2f57c99446730e6<SEP>chunk-6beab04bb204a738c7bc57c3d444cb13";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Ancestors are defined as deceased predecessors whose unresolved experiences are believed to influence future generations. They are revered entities in the context of honoring the departed and facilitating their transition.  

Ancestors are also discussed in the context of ancestral rituals and Mahal-e-amavasya observances, where they are venerated and their presence is invoked.  

Through their legacy, ancestors contribute to the human collective consciousness, influencing present suffering and transmitting their suffering through the collective.  

Additionally, ancestors collectively shape an individual’s emotional and psychological makeup, affecting personal identity and well-being.<SEP>Ancestors are mentioned as part of the generational information carried in cells.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Ancestors" .

