  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "The \"ancients in India\" are referenced as proponents of a simple principle related to health and well-being.<SEP>Ancient Indian sages or scholars who referred to consciousness as 'Chit' and contributed to the philosophical understanding of Chit Shakti.<SEP>The Ancients in India recognized five essential roles and attributes of a father in their cultural and philosophical traditions.<SEP>The ancients in India recognized five essential roles for a father, emphasizing his multifaceted contributions to a child's life.<SEP>The ancients in India are a group that observed and understood the life cycle and agricultural processes, as mentioned in the original text.<SEP>The ancients in India observed and conceptualized Karma through agricultural practices, linking actions to natural outcomes.<SEP>The ancients in India are referred to as proponents of philosophical teachings about karma and its mechanisms, particularly in the context of spiritual and moral law.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Ancients in India";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779721998"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

