<urn:mukthiguru:Attention> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-fda55ecccb000507a303d6e1d174ab3e<SEP>chunk-b9745746c3d492b20d6151c5ad818acf<SEP>chunk-2fcfdd09e7882fdd48ac5703861252ac<SEP>chunk-db13cb83fc521e55cec5df8eb2ee018c";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Attention is the act of focusing on something. It involves directing mental effort toward a specific object or activity, allowing an individual to prioritize that focus over other inputs. This definition captures the core idea that attention enables the individual to concentrate on a particular stimulus while filtering out distractions.

The concept is fundamental to cognition, as it underlies perception, learning, and decision-making. In various contexts, attention can be selective, divided, or sustained, reflecting different strategies for managing limited cognitive resources. The provided descriptions consistently define attention as the act of focusing on something, emphasizing the mental effort and prioritization involved.<SEP>Attention represents focus and awareness, which may wander during meditation.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Attention";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: RFx74Q6Oq2c (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RFx74Q6Oq2c)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cxgHFX04RtQ)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X3LKG0Ycl3A)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779728745"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

