  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and role descriptions, but the real content is about \"Awareness.\"

First, I need to identify the part that's relevant. The contaminated text starts with role and task descriptions, then instructions, and finally the input section. The input section has the entity name \"Awareness\" and a list of descriptions. Each description in the list is the same: \"Awareness involves conscious recognition and understanding of issues.\" There are five entries of this exact sentence.

Since the task is to extract the spiritual teaching or concept definition, I should focus on the repeated sentence. The developer instructions are all the parts about the role, task, input format, etc., which I need to remove. The key here is that the actual content is the definition of Awareness provided in the Description List. Even though the same sentence is repeated five times, the core concept is clear. There's no conflicting information here, just repetition. So the clean description should be that single sentence. I need to make sure not to include any of the surrounding instructions or role descriptions. The output should be just the definition in plain English, 1-4 sentences. Since there's only one unique sentence, that's the answer. No need to mention the repetition or anything else. Just the clean sentence.
</think>

Awareness involves conscious recognition and understanding of issues.""";
