  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "{\"Description\": \"{\\\"Description\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Description\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"We need to produce a merged description of the entity \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Beautiful States\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". The input includes a long description and multiple identical short descriptions. We must integrate all key information, be objective, third-person, mention the full name at the beginning, and keep within 600 tokens.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe have to handle conflicts: the short descriptions are consistent with the long one, so we can combine.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe must structure into multiple paragraphs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe must not exceed 600 tokens.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe must not add any extra formatting.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe must output plain text.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWe must not mention the short description? Actually, the short description is: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBut note: the long description does not mention that? Actually, the long description does not mention the short description. However, the input includes the short description as a separate JSON object.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBut the task says: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The description list is provided in JSON format. Each JSON object (representing a single description) appears on a new line within the `Description List` section.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSo we have two descriptions:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. The long description (the first JSON object) which is a meta-description about how to merge? Actually, the first JSON object is:\\\\\\\"}\\\"}\"}<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.<SEP>Beautiful states are positive mental conditions related to joy, love, and calm, associated with wise decisions.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

