<urn:mukthiguru:Bikes> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779251881"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-7c57553df2850654b5a35e1ee26c7149<SEP>chunk-b83c8b00df8935f2c00062b416bf9b2c<SEP>chunk-e1984cc91b0da578d9648e1604a3db60";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "culturaladoption";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Bikes are recommended for short-distance commuting as a low-fuel transportation option.<SEP>Using bicycles for short-distance commuting is highlighted as an eco-friendly alternative.<SEP>The Dutch are cited as a model for integrating bikes into daily commuting.`. This is actually a correct relationship. The entity `Dutch` is classified as `location` (incorrectly) and the relationship is correct. So, the main error is the classification of `Dutch`.<SEP>The Dutch are cited as a model for integrating bikes into daily commuting.` is fine. The entity `Dutch` is the problem.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Bikes";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)" .

