<urn:mukthiguru:Birth%20Ceremonies> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-9d8a8416ae7a083477cbb7ac15043bbb";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth. They are often performed by family members or religious leaders, reflecting cultural beliefs about the significance of birth. These ceremonies may include symbolic actions such as naming, blessing, or the presentation of gifts to the newborn and parents. The timing of the rituals typically coincides with the moment of birth, though variations exist across different traditions and regions.

In some cultures, birth ceremonies also involve the recitation of prayers or the use of specific objects to protect the infant. The exact form of the ceremony can vary widely, but the core purpose remains the same: to mark the transition of the newborn into the community and to invoke blessings for health and well-being. The diversity of practices underscores the central role of birth ceremonies in affirming cultural identity and communal bonds.<SEP>Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth.` - Correct.<SEP>Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth.` - Correct.<SEP>Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth.` - Correct.<SEP>Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth.` - Correct.<SEP>Birth ceremonies are spiritual rituals conducted at the time of birth.` - Correct.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779757103"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Birth Ceremonies";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "event" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Birthday%20Parties> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551902"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-25f394f47fe40575ea9fbcd110df6414<SEP>chunk-5f06ba1ae7a3d1eb5ae89a5a7db786f0<SEP>chunk-9eea478f3eb12a678ce672d3075c4af8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Birthday Parties are events enabled by community centers. They are recognized as social events that are celebrated by individuals and are discussed in the context of community activities. This indicates that birthday parties are a recognized category of events within community settings, falling under the range of activities offered by community centers.

Community centers support birthday parties as part of their event offerings, and they are among the events that community centers enable. The social nature of birthday parties is emphasized, with individuals gathering to celebrate, and these events are often mentioned in relation to community activities.

Therefore, birthday parties are both a type of event and a social activity that community centers facilitate, providing a venue for individuals to celebrate and interact within the community.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "event";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Birthday Parties" .

