  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Brahma Garbha refers to the ancient concept of limitless consciousness associated with the pineal, pituitary, and hypothalamus axes in the brain.<SEP>Brahma Garbha is described as the womb of limitless consciousness, associated with the pineal, pituitary, and hypothalamus axes in the brain.<SEP>Brahma Garbha refers to the womb of limitless consciousness as described by ancient Indian sages, associated with the pineal, pituitary, and hypothalamus axes in the brain.`<SEP>Brahma Garbha, or the womb of limitless consciousness, is an ancient concept associated with expanded consciousness and specific brain structures.<SEP>Brahma Garbha refers to the womb of limitless consciousness, associated with brain structures like the pineal, pituitary, and hypothalamus.<SEP>Brahma Garbha refers to the ancient Indian concept of limitless consciousness, discovered by sages and foundational to the mystical aspects of Soul Sync.<SEP>Brahma Garbha refers to the ancient concept of limitless consciousness, associated with brain structures such as the pineal, pituitary, and hypothalamus.";
