  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779648023"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "The \"broken mirror\" metaphor represents fragmented human identity caused by conflicting ideals, relationships, and existential uncertainty.<SEP>The broken mirror metaphor represents the fragmented and divided nature of human consciousness and society.<SEP>Broken Mirror serves as a metaphor for human beings' fragmented and divided nature.<SEP>The broken mirror serves as a metaphor for human beings' fragmented and imperfect nature, as analyzed in the video.<SEP>The original text mentions a \"broken mirror\" within the context of integration." .

