<urn:mukthiguru:Buddha> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Buddha";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779564551"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cI7D2aO34yw)<SEP>YouTube Video: UNdwPjyLGn0 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UNdwPjyLGn0)<SEP>YouTube Video: DmzZPgTh7_M (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DmzZPgTh7_M)<SEP>YouTube Video: 1_-cZz8YRFw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1_-cZz8YRFw)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Buddha, the historical and spiritual figure, is also regarded as a religious figure and a concept symbolizing enlightenment, inner peace, and balance. He exemplified compassion, as illustrated by tending to a wounded swan, and chose seclusion for spiritual enlightenment. As a spiritual teacher, he achieved enlightenment and taught the path to self-realization and awakening, emphasizing the realization of awakened consciousness and the illusion of self. His teachings stress inner peace, the transcendence of ego, and the potential for awakening in all beings, presenting a central figure in religious and philosophical discourse.

Buddha's teachings are inclusive, asserting that awakening is not exclusive to him, and he is presented as a central figure whose guidance is inclusive. He is also a concept that guides actions, embodying compassion and the pursuit of self-realization. Buddha symbolizes enlightenment, balance, and the need to transcend ego, as illustrated in the Thai story of mud obscuring enlightenment. He is referenced in the context of guiding actions and the grand vision.

Buddha is also described as a historical figure known for spiritual teachings, who experienced anger, and as a spiritual leader cited for teaching about the consequences of anger. In some narratives, Buddha demonstrated forgiveness through a silent smile after being spat on, and he is referenced in a story about handling anger and promoting self-compassion through mindful awareness. These anecdotes highlight his compassionate response to adversity.

Some descriptions focus on Buddha as the state of enlightenment or the ideal of achieving Buddhahood, while others emphasize his role in teaching about the consequences of anger. The incomplete description \"Budd\" is truncated and does not provide sufficient information for inclusion. Overall, Buddha is portrayed as a multifaceted figure whose teachings and actions embody compassion, forgiveness, and the pursuit of awakening.<SEP>Budd<SEP>Buddha is a spiritual leader""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-c300bba2ee34914195fc13be0187277e<SEP>chunk-8e03152ba26c428e5446f721ab8114a4<SEP>chunk-50a3afd25409a52a572d62a449dbc4ec<SEP>chunk-3ba320b05f330dd38ee53d270146e432<SEP>chunk-4d59e72aadbbf0c922fc8ed13db1693a<SEP>chunk-be5de8ed1db1e01f9ee5a260fb8d11ce<SEP>chunk-550e13cc834f4b3fe1d51617d1c42fa2<SEP>chunk-89ad31026dfac5cb5747676ec6d57a32<SEP>chunk-40b40d077b6b6ad2e3eb8995f7aa43cd<SEP>chunk-52d567ecc552b96b146755df515ac0bd<SEP>chunk-49ad825cb7cba993a98976aa8215c0f0<SEP>chunk-955183a7876a0d1c45e94af3baafdb73<SEP>chunk-353087e1120c5c6d7a54cec358cac19d<SEP>chunk-cb4fc2fbd442df7df8271a138eea2d39<SEP>chunk-205423882b48f788157f2fc6f5ec5467<SEP>chunk-abf954b4076fde8130baee4b61745658<SEP>chunk-9a50f8f9005c610dcbdc56af435e96a8<SEP>chunk-fdbf9aca2a79a0d5bef7d0b7c7804d67<SEP>chunk-a9818a0388e6c7fbe12a262f4b70178a<SEP>chunk-ea1f0fc5a4bd6b550f008cf8e4905da5<SEP>chunk-3907dc38c0d0edd5d39a312bc7148a7e<SEP>chunk-b580aa2839ef18f449209c7066e083d0<SEP>chunk-24b5f3611aa0088cf040177e4f897986" .

