  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Chanakya is a historical figure from ancient India mentioned in the text.<SEP>Chanakya is an ancient Indian scholar whose principles are cited regarding ideal marital partnerships.<SEP>Chanakya is an ancient Indian scholar referenced in the text for contextual accuracy.<SEP>Chanakya is an ancient Indian philosopher and royal advisor, traditionally attributed with authorship of the Manudharma Shastra.<SEP>Chanakya is a proper noun and is correctly capitalized in the text.<SEP>Chanakya is an ancient Indian scholar who advocated for marriages where men marry women from families of equal or lower stature to maintain dominance in partnerships.";
