<urn:mukthiguru:Christian%20Namaste> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bSyewSnu2Ak)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779255740"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-f02d58016cb210cdabb5a0e4e34489b9<SEP>chunk-fa4bb63d0902fb02ca5150a0e404f97c<SEP>chunk-9cae7143f497353be3068de2f13fe25c<SEP>chunk-a838d7152e4bebf83c9201b3d383a669<SEP>chunk-b1305ddb839be73a31e060addb9a200a<SEP>chunk-41070a47242b017794bd4b01d9403428<SEP>chunk-3f84526c0b3a657b3cc715347c2c1a58<SEP>chunk-52bc2f160d5933b804fba7010cd61529";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Christian Namaste";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Christian Namaste is a term that blends Christian and Indian cultural elements, as referenced in the closing of a text. It appears in the context of a revised chant and a corrected version, where it functions as a closing phrase symbolizing forgiveness and spiritual closure. The phrase is also described as a greeting that blends Christian and Indian traditions, embodying respect and spiritual connection.

Additionally, Christian Namaste is presented as a spiritual or religious concept, a mantra, or a blessing, often associated with forgiveness and support within a family. It is mentioned in the content as a term that may carry spiritual significance, and it is used in various contexts, including as a greeting, a closing phrase, and a spiritual concept. The phrase's usage spans across different parts of the text, indicating its multifaceted role in the narrative.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

