  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "City is the location where Diego holds annual talent search competitions, though its specific name is not provided.<SEP>The city where Sunil's daughter resides, where he decides to live part-time to maintain proximity to her.<SEP>A faceless urban environment where the young man feels insignificant and trapped in poverty.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "location";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-0c857ef7148c7fabda317a3a8fe52f05<SEP>chunk-f8449165361188bfe6afa260ab623922<SEP>chunk-369f0db74a66636fddaa77ce9a54b9b6";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "City" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Civilization> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Civilization is described as \"addicted\" due to systemic reliance on speed, thrill, and pleasure-seeking behaviors.<SEP>Civilization is described as addicted to speed, thrill, and pleasure, reflecting a low quality of consciousness.<SEP>A civilization that prioritizes external achievements and relationships as pathways to happiness.<SEP>Civilization is described as overvaluing information and motivation, neglecting the quiet mind.<SEP>A collective entity representing human society, characterized by self-dissatisfaction and societal pressures to conform to external role models.<SEP>The civilization is responsible for bringing up the younger ones and inculcating values.<SEP>A collective entity representing human society, characterized by self-dissatisfaction and societal pressures to conform to external role models.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Civilization";
