  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Colloquialism refers to informal language usage, such as \"went to\" in the text, contrasted with \"underwent\" for precision.<SEP>Informal language usage observed in the phrasing \"Discrimination and separation *is* no matter how you show it.\"<SEP>Colloquial language usage that may deviate from formal grammatical rules for natural speech.<SEP>The original sentence's use of \"is\" interpreted as a colloquial or informal phrasing despite grammatical inaccuracies.<SEP>The original sentence's use of \"is\" interpreted as a colloquial or informal phrasing despite grammatical inaccuracies.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
