<urn:mukthiguru:Communal%20Rights> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779717628"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cxgHFX04RtQ)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Communal Rights refer to collective entitlements and freedoms of groups within a society, pertaining to the rights of groups or communities. These rights are defined as the shared privileges and liberties that a community holds, which can become a source of unrest when threatened by hate speech. The concept emphasizes the collective nature of such entitlements, distinguishing them from individual rights, and highlights how external hostility, such as hate speech, can destabilize communal harmony.

When threatened by hate speech, communal rights can become a catalyst for social tension, serving as a protective framework for group identity while also acting as a potential flashpoint for conflict. This dual role underscores the delicate balance between safeguarding collective interests and maintaining social cohesion.

In summary, communal rights are collective entitlements and freedoms that define the shared privileges and liberties of groups, setting them apart from individual rights. They are vulnerable to external hostility, particularly hate speech, which can undermine communal harmony and provoke unrest. The protective aspect of communal rights must be carefully managed to prevent them from becoming sources of conflict.<SEP>Communal rights pertain to the rights of groups or communities.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-a37d3f6055e6d6441602d68de1d355d5<SEP>chunk-b9745746c3d492b20d6151c5ad818acf<SEP>chunk-70484d1909cf7a831cc47f5cf33a0709<SEP>chunk-13f1c611f4cbca7ca30788a6d47f7e15<SEP>chunk-2fcfdd09e7882fdd48ac5703861252ac<SEP>chunk-e13b3b3dd6b43643b1596294c861a1aa<SEP>chunk-3aae932faaf9adc0f11927ad30f84d81<SEP>chunk-67771372e5a1ccb6c8529ae33035d6e6";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Communal Rights" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Communal%20Violence> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: nUrc8O7Avvk (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Communal violence refers to conflicts arising from group divisions, often exacerbated by societal anxiety and differences in identity.<SEP>Communal violence refers to conflicts or hostility between groups based on shared identity, often exacerbated by social anxiety.<SEP>Communal violence refers to conflicts or hostility between groups based on shared identity, often exacerbated by social anxiety.";
