<urn:mukthiguru:Community> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6a2ca3b4a00fd65d72ac5932a227e2a8<SEP>chunk-cb2b247e069cff8e39d34db433289983<SEP>chunk-39ae671b46577f26845d7bb862a61c36<SEP>chunk-02f292000f544446b15f0519998d1dbc<SEP>chunk-faa6974a8318ba2e0ef63f3f66ff8ef6<SEP>chunk-2937f9db737764b56ab13c05271ce216<SEP>chunk-654ba1397813fb7e7e5aa81442780460<SEP>chunk-13115d12efdf6f06cb94255cf212ccfd<SEP>chunk-e1d5e0073f33e1ee1857e1f6302d5b7f<SEP>chunk-9eea478f3eb12a678ce672d3075c4af8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Community";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551791"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IGryscyFmV8)<SEP>YouTube Video: 4LIZkNHlNaM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4LIZkNHlNaM)<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Community is a multifaceted concept that encompasses both spiritual and social dimensions. It is often described as a group of people sharing a spiritual vision, providing collective support akin to a mother‑child bond, and embodying the interconnectedness of individuals working toward collective well‑being. In this view, community is seen as part of the universe, accepted without judgment, and as the ultimate form of change emerging from the breakdown of old systems such as government, medicine, and corporations, playing a central role in resolving problems and fostering peace.

However, community also carries negative connotations. It can refer to collective norms and traditions that impose expectations conflicting with personal fulfillment, and it may serve as a conduit for the transmission of violence. Additionally, community is recognized as a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices, shaping personal identity and actions.

Thus, community is simultaneously a source of mutual nurturing and spiritual solidarity, and a structure that can impose constraints and transmit harmful patterns. Its role in societal transformation and personal development remains contested, reflecting both its potential for collective empowerment and its capacity for oppression.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.<SEP>The community is a social group that interacts with and influences individual behaviors and practices.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Community%20Centers> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Community Centers are facilities constructed specifically for villages, providing free access to residents. These centers are designed to serve as communal spaces where people can gather for various activities without incurring costs.

In practice, Community Centers function as venues for social events and celebrations, such as marriages and birthdays. They are utilized to host these occasions, offering a suitable environment for such gatherings. The free nature of these centers ensures that all villagers can participate in community events without financial barriers.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Community Centers";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "artifact";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551884"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-25f394f47fe40575ea9fbcd110df6414<SEP>chunk-5f06ba1ae7a3d1eb5ae89a5a7db786f0" .

