<urn:mukthiguru:Comparison> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oalnb5-fHjY)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: _GEMrEWCiXw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_GEMrEWCiXw)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-3b972b1465c1099f09b7fe384e4ebabc<SEP>chunk-6ff356fa9f4583782a04af42a23a7935<SEP>chunk-ab8b9e8deff04b22db3cfe26b8508b88<SEP>chunk-f02b83f12f802c289fd8c9176c6dc8a9<SEP>chunk-2171a2444f1340eb8e26b9e8bb9ef9cc<SEP>chunk-6beab04bb204a738c7bc57c3d444cb13<SEP>chunk-15d5c49dad57bbf0bfa887044a164738<SEP>chunk-0cd54f605ef5308b827b0b4e872697da<SEP>chunk-3a5d8d7606e9b8e3d7ef11bf46090954<SEP>chunk-e27a47feac82bbd6f6606fd0582e97d1";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "We need to produce a comprehensive, cohesive summary of the entity \"Comparison\". The input is a list of JSON objects, each representing a description. The description list includes many entries, some duplicates, some nuanced. The task is to merge them into a single summary, multiple paragraphs, objective third-person, mention the full name of the entity at the beginning. Must not exceed 600 tokens. Must be in English. Must handle conflicts: there are duplicate descriptions (7 entries). Some are similar but with nuance: some talk about education system, self-commentary, self-criticism, societal/familial influences, cognitive behavior, social media, etc. Also some mention negative aspects (unhealthy, conflict). Some mention positive? Not really. The summary should integrate all key information: that comparison is an inherent cognitive function, conditioned by societal and familial influences, leading to evaluations between entities or ideas; it can be taught via education system, arises from self-commentary, self-criticism, and external systems like social media; it can be portrayed as inherently unhealthy, causing inner war, judgment, disconnection, affecting societal and economic dynamics; it's a fundamental cognitive behavior.\\n\\nWe need to produce a cohesive summary, maybe 2-3 paragraphs. Must be objective, third-person. Must mention the full name: \\\"Comparison\\\". Possibly \\\"Comparison (the entity)\\\" or \\\"Comparison (the relation)\\\". The entity is \\\"Comparison\\\". So we can start: \\\"Comparison is an inherent cognitive function...\\\"\\n\\nWe need to ensure we cover all points:\\n\\n- Education system teaches individuals to compare and judge others via test scores and rankings.\\n- Comparison arises from self-commentary and fuels inner war by evaluating aspects of life against idealized standards.\\n- Comparison involves evaluating oneself as superior to a partner, exacerbating judgment and disconnection.\\n- Comparison stems from self-criticism and the habit of evaluating experiences against idealized standards.\\n- Comparison is portrayed as inherently unhealthy, arising from confusion and hurt, and affecting societal and economic dynamics.\\n- Comparison is an inherent function of the mind, conditioned by societal and familial influences, leading to evaluations between entities or ideas.\\n- Comparison is an inherent function of the mind, conditioned by societal and familial influences, leading to evaluations between entities or ideas. (duplicate)\\n- Comparison is presented as a fundamental cognitive behavior shaped by external systems like social media and family dynamics.\\n\\nWe need to integrate these. Also note that some are contradictory: some say it's inherent, some say it's taught by education. But we can reconcile: it's both inherent and taught.\\n\\nWe need to handle conflicts: there are no distinct entities, just multiple descriptions of the same entity. So we can summarize each viewpoint but note that they are consistent.\\n\\nWe must not exceed 600 tokens. Let's count roughly: each token is about 0.75 words? Actually token is roughly 4 characters? But we can approximate. We'll aim for about 400-500 words.\\n\\nWe need to produce plain text, no extra formatting.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we mention the full name at the beginning.\\n\\nWe need to be objective, third-person.\\n\\nWe need to include all key information.\\n\\nWe need to handle the duplicate description: we can note that it's repeated.\\n\\nWe need to handle the negative portrayal: \\\"inherently unhealthy, arising from confusion and hurt, affecting societal and economic dynamics\\\".\\n\\nWe need to mention the role of education system: teaching to compare via test scores and rankings.\\n\\nWe need to mention self-commentary, self-criticism, evaluation against idealized standards.\\n\\nWe need to mention evaluation between entities or ideas.\\n\\nWe need to mention external systems like socia