\"Conflicts within families refer to disputes or tensions that arise among members of a family unit. According to the provided descriptions, these conflicts are commonly attributed to societal division and separation, which are broader societal structures that divide and separate individuals. The repeated and consistent statements across multiple sources reinforce this perspective, indicating that such conflicts are not isolated incidents but are linked to larger societal dynamics. Each description includes the qualifier “Seems correct.”, suggesting that the source perceives the explanation as accurate. The consensus view across the eight entries suggests that conflicts within families are rooted in these societal divisions and separations, and the source’s assessment of the explanation as correct is reflected in each description.\"

