<urn:mukthiguru:Confucius> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-843a288acbc9e654c4e8d31eb046a7fa<SEP>chunk-05a2f5d02725dc2dcf8ad2e755a9ea94<SEP>chunk-5d7bc721d374a5cb0cba9dd3f98f763b<SEP>chunk-83844586a5265192561cceab641ac4ba<SEP>chunk-0b93a19f07fdaada8a87bb7bfa37fae9<SEP>chunk-46f092e49beb29848499bc5cec4e1faf<SEP>chunk-f85d41f2377858e80129dfbf7af31bf8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real content about Confucius.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The contaminated text starts with instructions about producing a summary, handling conflicts, and integrating information. But the actual content about Confucius is in the description list. The key points there are about Confucius being a philosopher and teacher involved in a story about a stolen horse, where he judges a case and later reverses his decision based on the son's honesty. There's mention of conflicting accounts but they're part of the same story.

I need to remove all the developer instructions. The main spiritual teaching here is about Confucius's approach to honesty and justice in the stolen horse story. The conflicts mentioned are about different versions of the same story, but the core teaching is about the importance of honesty and the complexity in judgment. The user wants a clean 1-4 sentence description in plain English without any markdown. So I should focus on the essence of the story and the moral lesson without including the conflicting details as part of the teaching itself. The answer should be concise, just the spiritual content.
</think>

Confucius is a philosopher and teacher associated with parables exploring themes of honesty and justice. One story involves him judging a case where a boy stole a horse to feed his family, with conflicting accounts about the outcome: some versions claim Confucius reversed his decision based on the son's honesty, while others emphasize the ethical complexity of the situation. These variations reflect differing interpretations of his teachings on moral judgment and compassion.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779187351"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Confucius" .

