  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779753081"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Conscious Mind is defined as the part of the human mind that processes information and makes decisions in the present moment. This definition is consistently repeated across multiple descriptions, indicating a core understanding of the concept. Together, these descriptions reinforce the idea that the conscious mind is a key component of human cognition, responsible for immediate information processing and decision-making.

The description list is provided in JSON format, with each JSON object appearing on a new line. The first description appears to be a meta-commentary about the input format, stating that the input is a JSON object with a \"Description List\" section, but it is incomplete, ending with \"However, the input given is:\". The remaining six descriptions all state the same definition: the conscious mind processes information and makes decisions in the present moment. The consistency across the majority of the descriptions suggests that this definition is widely accepted or at least the most prominent in the provided data.<SEP>The conscious mind is the part of the human mind that processes information and makes decisions in the present moment.<SEP>The conscious mind is the part of the human mind that processes information and makes decisions in the present moment.<SEP>The conscious mind is the part of the human mind that processes information and makes decisions in the present moment.<SEP>The conscious mind is the part of the human mind that processes information and makes decisions in the present moment.""";
