<urn:mukthiguru:Culture> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779719904"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Culture";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fj2_d2lNGVk)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)<SEP>YouTube Video: EhY6npcnSs8 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EhY6npcnSs8)<SEP>YouTube Video: BZDXIQwOPdU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZDXIQwOPdU)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=77dJnbTCwsA)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "We need to produce a comprehensive, cohesive summary of the entity \"Culture\". The input is a list of description strings (JSON objects). We need to merge them into a single summary, multiple paragraphs, objective third-person, mention the full name of the entity at the beginning. Must not exceed 600 tokens. Must be in English. Must handle conflicts: some descriptions are contradictory (e.g., one says culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection, another says cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection, another says culture is another factor contributing to loneliness, another says culture refers to societal norms and practices that influence collective behavior and values, another says culture is a culture that believes in achieving happiness through external environmental changes and material success, another says culture refers to the collective practices and values developed through humanity's interaction with Earth and its resources, another says culture denotes a societal framework that values and actively promotes peace for all life and human beings, another says culture encompasses shared beliefs, values, and practices that shape societal expectations and ideals). So we have many definitions: culture as societal norms and practices influencing collective behavior and values; culture as a framework promoting peace; culture as shared beliefs, values, practices shaping expectations; culture as a belief system that achieves happiness through external changes; culture as a factor contributing to loneliness; culture as perpetuating misunderstandings about connection; culture as feeding misunderstanding of connection; culture as societal norms and practices that influence collective behavior and values.\\n\\nWe need to integrate all key information. We need to note conflicts: some descriptions are contradictory (e.g., culture as promoting peace vs culture as perpetuating misunderstandings). We can present both viewpoints with noted uncertainty.\\n\\nWe need to keep within 600 tokens. Let's count approximate tokens. We'll need to produce maybe 3-4 paragraphs.\\n\\nWe need to start with \\\"Culture is ...\\\" and then summarize.\\n\\nWe need to be objective, third-person.\\n\\nWe need to mention the full name: \\\"Culture\\\".\\n\\nWe need to handle conflicts: we can say \\\"Culture is a multifaceted concept; some descriptions emphasize its role in shaping collective behavior and values, while others highlight its potential to perpetuate misunderstandings or contribute to loneliness. Additionally, culture can be viewed as a framework promoting peace, or as a belief system focused on external success, or as a set of practices developed through interaction with Earth.\\\"\\n\\nWe need to ensure we include all key points:\\n\\n- Culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection in modern society.\\n- Cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection, perpetuating misconceptions about relationships.\\n- Culture is another factor contributing to loneliness.\\n- Culture refers to societal norms and practices that influence collective behavior and values.\\n- Culture is a belief system that believes in achieving happiness through external environmental changes and material success.\\n- Culture refers to collective practices and values developed through humanity's interaction with Earth and its resources.\\n- Culture denotes a societal framework that values and actively promotes peace for all life and human beings.\\n- Culture encompasses shared beliefs, values, and practices that shape societal expectations and ideals.\\n\\nWe need to integrate these.\\n\\nWe need to keep within 600 tokens. Let's approximate token count: each token roughly 1 word. So 600 tokens ~ 600 words. We'll produce maybe 250-300 words.\\n\\nWe need to output plain text, no extra formatting.\\n\\nWe need to start with \\\"Culture is ...\\\" and then paragraphs.\\n\\nWe need to mention the entity name at the beginning.\\n\\nWe need to handle conflicts: we can note that some descriptions present culture as a source of misunderstanding, while others present it as a promoter of peace, etc.\\n\\nWe need to be objective.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we don't omit any important facts.\\n\\nWe need to include all eight descriptions.\\n\\nWe need to be careful about the phrase \\\"Culture is another factor contributing to loneliness.\\\" That's a bit odd: \\\"another factor\\\" implies there are other factors, but we can just include it.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of shared beliefs, values, practices.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture can be a belief system that focuses on external success.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture can be a framework promoting peace.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture can be a set of practices developed through interaction with Earth.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal norm influencing collective behavior.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a factor contributing to loneliness.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal framework promoting peace.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of shared beliefs, values, practices shaping expectations.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a belief system focusing on external success.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of practices developed through interaction with Earth.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal norm influencing collective behavior.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a factor contributing to loneliness.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal framework promoting peace.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of shared beliefs, values, practices shaping expectations.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a belief system focusing on external success.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of practices developed through interaction with Earth.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal norm influencing collective behavior.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a factor contributing to loneliness.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal framework promoting peace.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of shared beliefs, values, practices shaping expectations.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a belief system focusing on external success.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of practices developed through interaction with Earth.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal norm influencing collective behavior.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a factor contributing to loneliness.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture perpetuates misunderstandings about connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that cultural influences feed misunderstanding of connection.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a societal framework promoting peace.\\n\\nWe need to incorporate the idea that culture is a set of shared beliefs, values, practices shaping expectations.\\n\\nWe need to inc