  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Ancient organisms buried in the ocean depths transformed into fossil fuels over millions of years, originally supporting life while alive.<SEP>Decomposed creatures are ancient organic life forms transformed into fossil fuels over millennia.<SEP>Decomposed creatures include bugs, birds, mammals, reptiles, plants, and trees that lived once and were buried under the sea, later transformed into fossil fuels.<SEP>Decomposed creatures refer to organic matter from decomposed organisms that contribute to energy production and sustainability.<SEP>Decomposed organic matter that contributes to manufacturing processes and everyday living through Mother Earth's womb.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Decomposed Creatures" .

