  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content about Dhara from the contaminated text. The text is a mix of developer instructions and JSON examples.

First, I need to look through the contaminated text. The main part that seems relevant is the JSON example provided. The key sentences are: \"Dhara is a name for the Earth goddess, reflecting cultural and spiritual reverence for nature.\" and \"Dhara is a personified deity or concept symbolizing the Earth, often associated with fertility and sustenance in cultural contexts.\"

These two sentences are the actual spiritual teachings. The rest of the text is either instructions for parsing JSON or repeated examples of the same structure. I need to remove all the developer talk and just keep the definitions of Dhara. Also, make sure there's no markdown and it's in plain English. Let me check if there's any other relevant info. The last part mentions integrating key information, which repeats the two points. So combining those two sentences into a concise description without any extra formatting. That should be it.
</think>

Dhara is a name for the Earth goddess, reflecting cultural and spiritual reverence for nature. She is also a personified deity or concept symbolizing the Earth, often associated with fertility and sustenance in cultural contexts.""";
