<urn:mukthiguru:Dharana> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779259850"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Dharana is a meditation technique that involves focusing one's attention on a specific form or essence to cultivate mental discipline. It is also understood as a spiritual concept that denotes contemplation or meditation, and within yoga and philosophical systems it is commonly associated with concentration and focus.

In many spiritual traditions, Dharana is described as a practice that may be combined with mantra, and it is recognized as a spiritual practice mentioned in various texts. The technique emphasizes focused attention or contemplation, often involving the visualization or contemplation of a deity or abstract concept. By concentrating on a particular object or idea, practitioners aim to deepen their meditative experience and enhance mental clarity. Dharana thus serves both as a method of meditation and as a broader philosophical notion of focused mental activity, integral to spiritual and yogic disciplines.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Dharana";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh61tFdyX8c)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)";
