  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "A disconnected person takes a path of destruction and hurt, leading to self-destructive behavior due to anger or frustration with their circumstances.<SEP>A disconnected person is characterized by pursuing destructive paths and being consumed by dissatisfaction." .

<urn:mukthiguru:Disconnected%20State> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779248121"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "A profound sense of disconnection from self and others, addressed through observation.<SEP>A disconnected state reflects isolation or lack of purpose, leading to fragmented work relationships and internal conflict.<SEP>Disconnected state describes a mindset where love shown by others cannot be experienced.<SEP>A psychological or emotional state where an individual is detached or unresponsive to external stimuli, impacting their perception of affection.<SEP>A state where emotional barriers prevent love from being experienced by another person.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Disconnected State";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GfAMCHC6_ek)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-468fc234a44cb0396e4202675d40e771<SEP>chunk-b46675c05bfa30223c5b090123b0a08b<SEP>chunk-d1580b380e66d60231e8bb1500c438e9<SEP>chunk-7876881b163cb9e8fd183208ace12836<SEP>chunk-69c518552350983af20c342ffe0b1ce1" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Disconnection> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Disconnection is a multifaceted concept describing a state of separation that undermines genuine presence and empathy in relationships. It can arise from self‑obsessed consciousness, judgmental behavior, and negative emotions such as possessiveness or insecurity, leading to relational breakdowns and emotional or physical separation from others. Disconnection may also be viewed as a process of emotional detachment that can progress through stages if not managed, and it can be experienced personally, as in Sunil’s relationship with his father, and at a societal level as a fragmented condition of humanity that contributes to collective suffering. It is linked to depression, exacerbated by modern habits like isolated eating and digital distraction, and can cause loneliness and distance. The condition is avoided by conscious wealth creators and is described as a state of emotional or physical separation from others, often caused by negative behaviors or emotions, and as emotional or relational distance between individuals stemming from insecurity or possessiveness. At a higher level, disconnection between self and others diminishes in the second level of oneness, and living in suffering results in broken relationships with people and life.<SEP>Disconnection describes emotional or relational distance between individuals, caused by negative states like possessiveness or insecurity.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-a813939f321629f8537b01c0cc6653ae<SEP>chunk-98a858d2ad9db1fe93167a9194441c7b<SEP>chunk-ab8b9e8deff04b22db3cfe26b8508b88<SEP>chunk-fa73522aa96594208b9f43ea66a6493e<SEP>chunk-5f6e567050111ca1e6e0891a182bd7b3<SEP>chunk-b0b6f9f02020768407fee531e6074a4d<SEP>chunk-a77f1fee05f090e6b596f48781d6d33a<SEP>chunk-b4387a01e271d1d16068a0288faa84e5<SEP>chunk-5c8f3b58191cd7eb20e97c7adfd8085c<SEP>chunk-e267787286890ad0751663f8a3e06d5c<SEP>chunk-b19b2a822951a545ded34a82295b89dc<SEP>chunk-f75c5d6ff6cf90a0c79623ead0773fbc<SEP>chunk-8c47a43e466f805ea381f194db0fb072<SEP>chunk-5df4284d1aa76cb89d7850ba8ee300b9<SEP>chunk-5a1740daf11f031bb2f4e4877b90a316<SEP>chunk-8b7b22cfd463021890139fccede91731<SEP>chunk-37a50ba57b87bf8d444df3da83283e84<SEP>chunk-428c28379181a7cdc217fc69118ccc4d";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779687753"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Disconnection";
