<urn:mukthiguru:Domain-Specific%20Names> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Domain-Specific Names are terms that are particular to a specific field, requiring careful attention to avoid errors. Because they are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms, they are often targeted for refinement to ensure accuracy and consistency within their respective domains. The correction process involves refining these names to improve precision and reduce the risk of misinterpretation, thereby supporting the overall reliability of technical discourse. By addressing the misuse of domain-specific terms, the correction effort aims to maintain clarity and reliability in technical communication. Domain-Specific Names serve both as identifiers of specialized concepts and as subjects of correction to maintain clarity and reliability in technical communication. Their refinement ensures that terminology remains precise and consistent, which is essential for accurate knowledge transfer and collaborative work across disciplines.

The focus on correction highlights the importance of precise terminology in specialized contexts, where misuse can lead to misunderstandings or errors. Multiple descriptions consistently identify Domain-Specific Names as a focus area for correction, involving specific terms. The correction effort aims to maintain clarity and reliability in technical communication, ensuring that terminology remains precise and consistent across disciplines.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.<SEP>Domain-Specific Names are a focus area for correction, involving specific terms.""";
