<urn:mukthiguru:Dr.%20Andrew%20Newberg> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Dr. Andrew Newberg";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-4b1b158579ce0e632c723f5212472e9c<SEP>chunk-0ff8600d1eb0818e8deb9d5aab2e4351<SEP>chunk-a2cc4d07b96d813e34cd5ee5e3d96e0d<SEP>chunk-2984b976f037a27596b29e94de8e3b21<SEP>chunk-ba8be2f785637451bf56a7dc7363715b<SEP>chunk-b694dcc1bb7e7bd6fa7878c3592e7c19<SEP>chunk-f1fcfd5a753f74e11984fed8934aec32<SEP>chunk-3f7b8834c0b5fdd9d0b5f928c5733a2b";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779188244"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Dr. Andrew Newberg is a neuroscientist, neuropsychiatrist, and researcher whose work bridges neuroscience and the study of religious and spiritual experiences. He is best known as a co‑author of the book “How God Changes Your Brain,” which explores the neurological impact of spiritual practices. Newberg’s interdisciplinary approach has earned him recognition for linking brain function with concepts such as consciousness, meditation, and the physiological effects of religious rituals.

His research encompasses a range of topics, including the effects of meditation on brain function, breathing techniques, and the enhancement of brain efficiency through conscious repetitive hand movements. Newberg has also investigated the neurological effects of Soul Sync, a practice that combines focused attention with specific hand gestures, reporting that it can improve memory formation and overall brain performance. Additionally, he has contributed to the scientific understanding of how meditation influences neural pathways and cognitive processes.

Newberg’s scholarly output includes co‑authoring research on the impact of meditation on brain function and has been cited for his studies on the physiological changes associated with spiritual practices. He is recognized for supporting the neurological effects of Soul Sync, providing evidence that such practices can enhance brain efficiency and memory. His work continues to be referenced in discussions of the intersection between neuroscience and spirituality.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

