<urn:mukthiguru:Drug%20Addiction> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Drug Addiction";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551877"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-e2bd3f4cf43dab42e9cb72ed41ed496d<SEP>chunk-287b5379ffe15e81cc3508670d4597aa<SEP>chunk-29187c924e9a374fb8f3996bb7bb3fb9<SEP>chunk-25f394f47fe40575ea9fbcd110df6414<SEP>chunk-5f06ba1ae7a3d1eb5ae89a5a7db786f0";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Drug addiction is a chronic, relapsing condition characterized by compulsive use of psychoactive substances despite harmful effects. It is categorized as a classical addiction with severe societal and health consequences, and it pertains to substance abuse involving illicit or prescription drugs, contributing to physical and psychological harm.

Drug addiction is also cited as a rising crisis linked to societal disintegration and as a rising social issue requiring state intervention.

The societal consequences of drug addiction are profound, often leading to disintegration of communities and increased burden on healthcare systems. The condition's chronic nature means that relapse is common, making sustained treatment essential. Public health responses typically involve state-led interventions, including prevention programs, treatment services, and policies aimed at reducing the availability of harmful substances.

In summary, drug addiction is a multifaceted problem that combines chronic, relapsing behavior with severe health and societal consequences. It is driven by the misuse of psychoactive substances, both illicit and prescription, and is increasingly recognized as a rising crisis tied to societal disintegration. Effective responses require state-led interventions, including prevention, treatment, and policy measures, to mitigate its impact on individuals and communities.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8mmungGgDNw)<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)" .

