  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Duryodhana is a character from the Mahabharata who harbored resentment and anger due to perceived injustice in inheritance.<SEP>Duryodhana is a character marked by childhood anger and jealousy, which evolved into resentment and hate towards his cousins, leading to a desire for revenge.<SEP>Duryodhana is associated with a faction that desired war, contributing to inevitable conflict alongside Dharma Raja's side.<SEP>Duryodhana is a key antagonist in the Mahabharata, associated with the refusal of Pandavas' rightful kingdom.`" .

