<urn:mukthiguru:Energy> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Energy is a concept representing the flow of influence from states, affecting intention, decisions, and actions.<SEP>Energy is a fundamental aspect of the field, representing its dynamic and active nature.<SEP>Energy is mentioned as being initially high due to anger or frustration but later destructive.<SEP>Energy signifies the initial surge of power or motivation driven by anger or frustration, which later diminishes as addictions take hold.<SEP>Energy represents the capacity of a person to act, which can be directed towards destructive or constructive purposes depending on one's mindset.<SEP>Energy refers to the dynamic force within the program that fosters connection and growth.<SEP>Vital force that can either be dissipated (in stressful states) or focused (in beautiful states), influencing mental clarity and engagement with life.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Vr3PS2DdbDU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vr3PS2DdbDU)<SEP>YouTube Video: AyUE-2Uh5Vg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AyUE-2Uh5Vg)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: odNtpKqbCQo (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odNtpKqbCQo)<SEP>YouTube Video: aqSM9LwqWgA (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aqSM9LwqWgA)<SEP>YouTube Video: U23yKxWbIcI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U23yKxWbIcI)";
