<urn:mukthiguru:Eye%20Consciousness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779647095"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-f72de7c8d762c18a6655f15c49149836<SEP>chunk-7dca0f22171b9785fbbab01b79ee3fa3<SEP>chunk-1d104bf7b587259887bc9a25750b3a02<SEP>chunk-5750a413a72601ce81e6195a148e09ad<SEP>chunk-acd33e9d80650cd874ca18c3457f81a6<SEP>chunk-1a41bff298d480e5ee5d61353c7e062c";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: mmpmX3-qfc4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mmpmX3-qfc4)<SEP>YouTube Video: _GEMrEWCiXw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_GEMrEWCiXw)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Eye Consciousness is a state of divided, separated, self‑centered awareness marked by destructive emotions such as anger and stress, feelings of loneliness, and persistent judgments. It is characterized by internal conflict and a preoccupation with the self, which limits an individual's perception of interconnectedness with others and the broader environment.

This condition drives a perception in which people view others as competitors or enemies, fostering disturbance, anxiety, and heightened stress. The resulting state is a fragmented consciousness that separates the self from others, leading to a sense of isolation and a distorted view of relationships. Overall, Eye Consciousness reflects a self‑centered, conflicted mindset that undermines holistic awareness and promotes negative interpersonal dynamics.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Eye Consciousness" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Eyebrow%20Center> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6254a0998449b5aae9f36e202e6ddd4f<SEP>chunk-510c74de625674a35dffb4f0f8a8acb0<SEP>chunk-2946fd6f690a4f147698b0825594b6df<SEP>chunk-48f438418db1330dddb1b4a3303306e1<SEP>chunk-511a319a40b03fc2d48c14b1ec8da740<SEP>chunk-43e5b5923e8d509b9e9edf60b61ff56b<SEP>chunk-4c6054ccc3bee7f9d86c600fc50b5dc7";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "naturalobject";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real spiritual teachings about the Eyebrow Center.

First, I need to identify the key points from the descriptions. The JSON objects mention that the Eyebrow Center is between the eyebrows, used in meditation, visualization, awareness, focus, observing emotions, shifting awareness, and visualizing a \"golden lotus blossom\" for abundance and creativity. There are also mentions of different traditions like meditation and practices for focus.

I need to synthesize these into a concise summary. The instructions say to start with the full name, mention it's an anatomical reference point, then cover its uses in meditation, visualization, awareness, observing emotions, shifting awareness, and the golden lotus blossom visualization. Also, note that it's part of various traditions.

I should avoid any developer notes, like the token count or formatting requirements. Just the clean spiritual content. Let me check if all the key points are covered: location, uses in meditation and visualization, awareness, emotions, shifting awareness, golden lotus for abundance and creativity, and mention of various traditions. Yes, that's all there. Now, structure it into 1-4 sentences without bullet points or headers. Make sure it's plain English and flows naturally.
</think>

Eyebrow Center is a specific anatomical reference point located between the eyebrows, used in meditation and awareness practices as a focal point for visualization, attention, and emotional observation. It serves to shift awareness, concentrate focus, and in some traditions, visualize a \"golden lotus blossom\" to manifest abundance and creativity. This concept appears across various meditation and awareness traditions, emphasizing its role in both spiritual and practical techniques.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779552331"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
