  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "event";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779665492"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Father's Day is a recent tradition celebrated on the third Sunday of June. The day is dedicated to fostering healing and connection between fathers and children, emphasizing the importance of familial bonds that extend beyond biological relationships.

It honors both biological fathers and father figures, including those who provided paternal support. By expanding the definition of fatherhood beyond biological ties, Father's Day recognizes a broader spectrum of paternal influence, encompassing non‑biological father figures who contribute to the family's well‑being.

The tradition seeks to strengthen ties within families and highlight the diverse ways fatherhood can be expressed. Through this celebration, the day promotes a more inclusive understanding of paternal roles, acknowledging the impact of paternal support on children's development and the healing of relationships.<SEP>Father's Day is a day to celebrate fathers, reflect on paternal relationships, and express gratitude for their contributions.<SEP>Father's Day is a day to remember fathers, reflect on relationships, and express gratitude for their contributions. It honors both biological fathers and father figures in one's life.<SEP>Father's Day is an event celebrating fathers and expressing gratitude to those who have played the role of a father.<SEP>Father's Day is an event where individuals are encouraged to perform three specific actions to honor and connect with their fathers, fostering mutual cherishing.<SEP>Father's Day is an event celebrated to honor fathers, with suggested activities to strengthen familial bonds.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Father's Day" .

