<urn:mukthiguru:Fear> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779687808"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and multiple descriptions of the entity \"Fear\". My job is to sift through all that and pull out the real spiritual content.

First, I need to identify the key points from the descriptions. The long first description mentions Fear as multifaceted, dissolving with truth, linked to unaddressed problems, and contrasting with enlightenment. It also talks about Fear's dual nature, societal pressures, and its role in motivating achievements. There's mention of Fear being a core emotion alongside anger and suffering, and even affecting food and eaters. 

Then there are shorter descriptions: Fear as the fundamental emotion, liberation from it in enlightenment, all fears rooted in fear of death, Fear used as a tool for violence causing division, and Fear creating anxiety affecting relationships. 

I need to integrate these without contradictions. The main spiritual concepts here are Fear's role in human experience, its contrast with enlightenment, the idea that all fears stem from fear of death, and how Fear can lead to division or anxiety. The part about food and eaters seems odd and might be a mistake or irrelevant, so maybe exclude that. Also, the mention of Fear as a motivator for achievements and self-worth validation is more psychological but still part of the spiritual context here.

I should combine these into a coherent 1-4 sentence description. Start by stating Fear's multifaceted nature, its contrast with enlightenment, the root in fear of death, its dual role in motivating and causing division, and its impact on relationships and anxiety. Avoid the technical parts and conflicting points. Make sure it's plain English, no bullet points, and just the clean description.
</think>

Fear is a multifaceted psychological and existential condition characterized by insecurity, societal pressures, and unresolved issues that accumulate into persistent anxiety.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JwMlR98BgrI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hwNlLB1sze0)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oc5ar2g2rnI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fj2_d2lNGVk)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GfAMCHC6_ek)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bSyewSnu2Ak)<SEP>YouTube Video: QAnRefsK-3Y (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QAnRefsK-3Y)<SEP>YouTube Video: uSAO5p0GIU8 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uSAO5p0GIU8)<SEP>YouTube Video: XFFgRTgP8Rs (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XFFgRTgP8Rs)<SEP>YouTube Video: ajMAwlKh3YM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajMAwlKh3YM)<SEP>YouTube Video: YkIBYppBtro (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YkIBYppBtro)<SEP>YouTube Video: Lst4MvxPCx4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lst4MvxPCx4)<SEP>YouTube Video: 1_-cZz8YRFw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1_-cZz8YRFw)<SEP>YouTube Video: ffhDTzE4nDU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ffhDTzE4nDU)<SEP>YouTube Video: cHAJiF2byzg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cHAJiF2byzg)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W2ZzApmqJmo)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XMzZe5aEmTo)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oZRQoiRe7s4)";
