  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real content.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The contaminated text is about \"Focus Areas\" which are described as correction priorities for text. The components mentioned are homophones/misheard words, domain-specific terminology, punctuation, capitalization, and readability adjustments. The purpose is improving readability and clarity.

The user's instructions say to remove all developer stuff like role descriptions, prompt templates, and meta-text. So I need to look for the actual definition. The draft provided in the contaminated text seems to be the cleaned version, but I need to check if that's part of the real content or just part of the developer's example.

Looking at the contaminated text, the key points are in the \"Key points to include\" section and the draft. The real content is the definition of Focus Areas as correction priorities targeting those components. The developer's instructions are about how to structure the summary, token count, etc., which should be removed.

So the clean description should be the draft provided, but without any of the developer's notes. The draft starts with \"Focus Areas are a set of correction priorities...\" and continues. That's the actual content. The rest is instructions on how to create it, which needs to be stripped out.

I need to make sure there's no mention of the process, like token counting or structuring paragraphs. Just the definition. The final answer should be a 1-4 sentence plain English description. The draft fits that, so I'll extract that part.
</think>

Focus Areas are a set of correction priorities targeting homophones/misheard words, domain-specific terminology, punctuation, capitalization, and readability adjustments to enhance text clarity and accuracy. These components ensure proper text correction and are consistently emphasized across descriptions as essential""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779700940"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

