<urn:mukthiguru:Grammatical%20Error> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2z5qxSr4EaI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fdPQxZsPAwI)<SEP>YouTube Video: smrj15-QOAI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=smrj15-QOAI)<SEP>YouTube Video: nUrc8O7Avvk (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vIUY446FVPw)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0u9oe-5HPmk)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-791613ee96d428f562709fadee905618<SEP>chunk-ac963c80865bf4f33baf1d166cbe42de<SEP>chunk-6ccd1f5debd2817e69e48d59df4cdf36<SEP>chunk-576f10f06b7632e1972cb071c6564b42<SEP>chunk-c3bdf300b2509154604072df1057a411<SEP>chunk-c32bf7fcfe6dd8d2fa78dd2f0cb30726<SEP>chunk-8e15fc85d32ce342ec9c480484b3580f";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Grammatical Error is a mistake in language that violates the rules of syntax, morphology, or punctuation, leading to awkward phrasing, incorrect subject‑verb agreement, improper article usage, missing verbs, or sentence fragments. Such errors can disrupt the coherence of a text and affect readability. They may arise in articles, transcripts, videos, or any written material.

Specific examples include an article that misuses articles with engines, awkward phrasing such as “We are not being capable” and “how we manage our life,” and a correction from singular ‘life’ to plural ‘lives.’ Other issues involve an awkward phrasing with a misplaced colon and incorrect verb tense, and a subject‑verb agreement error in the sentence “Discrimination and separation is no matter how you show it,” where the compound subject requires a plural verb. Errors in the video’s text also appear, such as incorrect grammar and awkward phrasing, and broader categories like improper punctuation, missing verbs, or sentence fragments that disrupt text coherence.

The list of descriptions also notes duplicate entries for the subject‑verb agreement issue, indicating that the same example appears twice. No conflicting information about distinct entities was identified; the variations are all within the same grammatical error context. Some descriptions also mention that grammatical errors can involve multiple types simultaneously, such as a combination of punctuation and missing verbs.

Overall, grammatical errors are defined by their capacity to impair clarity and flow, and they can manifest in various forms across different media, including articles, transcripts, and video text. Addressing these errors typically involves revising phrasing, correcting agreement, fixing punctuation, and ensuring proper verb usage to restore coherence.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Grammatical Error";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779735001"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

