<urn:mukthiguru:Grandparents> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-aaa5c02ef780f417e1e3498aff83c60b<SEP>chunk-3508c1cccdf21436532772d00c3c3463<SEP>chunk-4be5f58baaab4360b84499e4e9c8f89b<SEP>chunk-f11387cad436a638d2f57c99446730e6<SEP>chunk-6beab04bb204a738c7bc57c3d444cb13<SEP>chunk-b2b3f4e0ec4ca323c0c90b860c94bdb5<SEP>chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef<SEP>chunk-f8d4df49e2bb59337f3b12dcef1d6f2c";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Grandparents";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779656816"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Grandparents are individuals who, across human societies, contribute to the transmission of emotions and behaviors across generations. They are also referenced in the context of individuality and generational information, serving as key figures in the social and cultural continuity of families.

Historically, grandparents have played a critical role in child‑rearing, influencing genetic traits for longevity and thereby affecting the health and lifespan of subsequent generations.

In hunter‑gatherer societies, grandparents assume a crucial nurturing role, caring for children when parents are occupied with survival tasks, ensuring the continuity of the group and the well‑being of the young.<SEP>Grandparents in human societies historically played a critical role in child-rearing, influencing genetic traits for longevity.<SEP>Grandparents in hunter-gatherer societies play a crucial role in nurturing children when parents are occupied with survival tasks.<SEP>Grandparents in human societies historically played a critical role in child-rearing, influencing genetic traits for longevity.<SEP>Grandparents in hunter-gatherer societies play a crucial role in nurturing children when parents are occupied with survival tasks.<SEP>Grandparents refers to the elder generation in human societies, historically responsible for nurturing children due to parental occupational demands.""" .

