We should avoid repeating \"suitable for both seasoned practitioners and beginners\" and \"often preferred by beginners\" too many times. We can combine.

We should avoid repeating \"as discussed in the content\" and \"contrasted with solo practice\" too many times. We can mention them once.

We should avoid repeating \"structured meditation sessions with external guidance\" and \"structured meditation practices\" and \"external guidance\" too many times. We can use \"structured meditation sessions with external guidance\" and then \"external guidance\" is redundant? Actually, we can say \"structured meditation sessions with external guidance\" and then \"external guidance\" is part of that. We can avoid repeating \"external guidance\" by using \"guided\" or \"with guidance\".

