<urn:mukthiguru:Heartlessness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Heartlessness is a term that can refer to two distinct concepts. In one sense, heartlessness is condemned when humans engage in actions toward elephants and the environment that are callous or indifferent. This usage highlights moral disapproval of behavior that disregards the welfare of animals and ecological systems.

In another sense, heartlessness describes the inability of a leader to empathize with others' pain. This definition emphasizes a personal or professional deficiency where a leader fails to recognize or respond to the suffering of those affected by their decisions. Both senses of the term underscore a lack of compassion, though they apply to different contexts: one to broader societal and environmental actions, the other to individual leadership behavior.<SEP>Heartlessness is the inability of a leader to empathize with others' pain.<SEP>Heartlessness is the inability of a leader to empathize with others' pain.<SEP>Heartlessness is the inability of a leader to empathize with others' pain.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779719902"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VTx4G0KEuUE)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=77dJnbTCwsA)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-fbc362953fe784a8510b72471b749390<SEP>chunk-e22181d45ff680a216a2e1e3bb46c19d";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Heartlessness" .

