  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """{\"Description\": \"Entity Name: Humanity\\n\\nDescription List:\"}
{\"Description\": \"Humanity represents the collective human consciousness needing a shift towards Oneness.\"}
{\"Description\": \"The term \\\"Humanity\\\" is capitalized in the original text but should be lowercase \\\"humanity\\\" as it refers to the general concept.\"}
{\"Description\": \"Humanity refers to all human beings collectively facing the problem of divisiveness and requiring a shift towards Oneness.\"}
{\"Description\": \"The collective human population, whose consciousness is targeted by the concept of Oneness for promoting unity.\"}
{\"Description\": \"The collective human population, whose consciousness is targeted by the concept of Oneness for promoting unity.\"}
{\"Description\": \"Humanity refers to all human beings collectively and is associated with addressing global challenges.\"}
{\"Description\": \"Humanity represents the collective human population and its shared consciousness.\"}<SEP>Humanity is referenced in discussions about collective fear and the pursuit of freedom.<SEP>Humanity refers to all human beings collectively, currently facing crises due to self-centered behavior and unwise signals.<SEP>Humanity is a collective entity representing all human beings, currently facing global crises and environmental challenges.<SEP>Humanity refers to the collective existence of humans sharing evolutionary history and interconnectedness across genetic, neurological, mental, emotional, and spiritual dimensions.<SEP>Collective term for all human beings, responsible for actions affecting the environment and other living beings.<SEP>Collective existence of humans as interconnected and inseparable.""";
