<urn:mukthiguru:I-Consciousness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "I-Consciousness";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-35e48385a0a3608b5da5a16afae83eaa<SEP>chunk-c6d1ac7b77c644cdbe0e473d070e10a0<SEP>chunk-a6edb23148812a00c784704ababdb3ee<SEP>chunk-18fa3a7d8837c4f0b21f7ce5e53f50b2<SEP>chunk-bcbe9d15ce49d684cccca9bf4b6bb70a<SEP>chunk-baf2b6300d9383f209a9838b89760571<SEP>chunk-0a965090c99c9c63ccbf84e7a2e66878<SEP>chunk-07bbbe415fc6ff4eb6e48c047d81efd5";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779188025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching about \"I-Consciousness\" from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and notes, so I need to sift through that to find the real content.

First, I'll look at the descriptions listed. The first point says I-consciousness is a state of self-obsessed thinking leading to destructive emotions. The second mentions destructive states like anger, fear, and a desire to control. The third contrasts it with One-Consciousness. The fourth calls it a limited self-centered awareness. The fifth and sixth talk about generating bad energy and pollution. The seventh mentions transformation into collective consciousness through energy shifts. The eighth repeats the self-obsessed state and harmful behaviors.

The developer notes mention integrating all key info, contrasting with One-Consciousness, and including elements like bad energy, pollution, and transformation. They also note that all descriptions refer to the same entity except One-Consciousness.

So, the main points are: I-Consciousness is self-centered, leads to destructive emotions and harmful actions, generates bad energy, is contrasted with One-Consciousness, and can transform into collective consciousness through energy shifts. I need to combine these into a concise, clean description without any developer jargon. Make sure to mention the full name at the beginning, keep it objective, and structure it in a few sentences. Avoid bullet points and headers. Let me piece that together.
</think>

I-Consciousness is a self-obsessed state of individual awareness characterized by self-centered thinking, destructive emotions like anger, fear, and discontent, and a desire to control or dominate. It generates harmful behaviors, limited self-perception, and is associated with negative energy or \"pollution.\" Contrasted with One-Consciousness, it represents a restricted form of awareness that can transform into collective consciousness energy through personal and communal shifts.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLVPL1dXKc0)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

