<urn:mukthiguru:Ignorance> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: uvhEf3ToMHI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uvhEf3ToMHI)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551396"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Ignorance is a condition characterized by the lack of knowledge or awareness regarding life's fundamental truths. It encompasses the mistaken belief that material success alone leads to happiness and that liberation from suffering is unattainable. According to the sources, ignorance is also a state of not knowing, which the text identifies as a form of suffering that must be dispelled.

Recognizing and overcoming these misconceptions is essential for achieving a deeper understanding of life's realities. The concept underscores that dispelling ignorance is necessary for personal growth and for attaining a more accurate perception of the world.<SEP>Ignorance is a state of not knowing, which the text describes as a form of suffering that must be dispelled.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-0b3b9413e3a4acbecc07f577488e54e4<SEP>chunk-8f956406c1498a0f42494ef30d6087a0";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Ignorance";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

