  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Inclusive Thinking";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Inclusive thinking involves embracing diversity and interconnectedness in decision-making to address systemic exploitation.<SEP>Emphasizes unity in thought and action to end exploitation and economic unrest.<SEP>Inclusive thinking emphasizes unity in cognitive and behavioral patterns to transcend exploitative paradigms.<SEP>A paradigm advocating for unity in thought and action to eliminate exploitation and foster collective well-being.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779420717"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

<urn:mukthiguru:Inclusive%20and%20cause%20good%20to%20you%20and%20others> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779748653"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Inclusive and cause good to you and others";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching from the contaminated text. The contaminated text has a lot of developer instructions and JSON structure, but I need to focus on the real content.

First, I'll look through the text. The main entity is \"Inclusive and cause good to you and others\". The descriptions mention that the term is correctly written, conveys inclusivity and doing good, promotes a positive mindset, and encourages actions benefiting individuals and communities. There's also talk about the term being used to foster inclusivity and generate goodwill. The rest seems to be instructions on how to process the data, like token counts and formatting, which I should ignore.

I need to make sure I only include the spiritual content. The key points are the term's meaning, its purpose in promoting inclusivity and goodwill, and its role in benefiting both individuals and communities. The part about the description list being identical and reinforcing accuracy is part of the developer notes, so I should exclude that. Also, the instructions about token counts and formatting are irrelevant here.

Putting it all together, the clean description should be a concise summary of the term's meaning and purpose without any extra details. Let me check if I missed anything. The entity name is mentioned at the beginning, and the main concepts are covered. Alright, that should do it.
</think>

Inclusive and cause good to you and others is a term that conveys inclusivity and the act of doing good for oneself and others. It promotes a positive, inclusive mindset and encourages actions that benefit both individuals and the community, fostering inclusivity and generating goodwill toward others. The term has been accurately expressed in written form, with consistent descriptions reinforcing its correct usage and emphasizing its role in encouraging communal and personal well-being.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6052761888817e6a639d7d02535dd8c5" .

