  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching from the contaminated text. The text has a lot of developer instructions and repeated points.

First, I need to identify the key spiritual content. The main points mentioned are that Incompleteness is a concept related to partial engagement in activities like eating, relating, or meditating. This partial engagement leads to diminished bliss and lack of totality in experiences. The repeated statements reinforce this definition.

I should remove all the developer notes like \"We need to produce...\" and the instructions about formatting. The core idea is that partial participation reduces the quality of experiences. The entity name is Incompleteness, and the concept is about how not fully engaging in activities affects one's sense of completeness and bliss.

I need to condense this into 1-4 sentences without bullet points. Make sure it's in plain English and third-person. Let me check if there's any other spiritual content. The repeated parts all circle back to the same idea, so the main points are covered. No other concepts are mentioned. Alright, time to put it together concisely.
</think>

Incompleteness is a concept describing partial engagement in activities like eating, relating, or meditating. Such partial participation diminishes bliss and results in a lack of totality or completeness in experiences. The concept emphasizes that full involvement is necessary to achieve totality and optimal quality in experiences.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-20d55a95f1cbc94a40998bcd62b8a62f<SEP>chunk-421a4c58520d1e933d3bc17c203cc893";
