  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Any state of inner disturbance is referred to as stress, encompassing states like anger, fear, and loneliness.<SEP>Inner disturbance is alleviated through connection via conscious efforts to help others.<SEP>Inner disturbance refers to a state of emotional or mental turmoil that negatively affects individuals and contributes to global suffering.<SEP>Inner disturbance refers to a state of emotional or psychological unrest that requires conscious attention to prevent escalation.<SEP>Inner disturbance refers to emotional or psychological turmoil that requires conscious attention to prevent escalation.<SEP>Inner disturbance is a state experienced by individuals.";
