<urn:mukthiguru:Input%20Text> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zp2w7DTmOwc)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=owXqW04b08o)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Mr1cjAz2y9I (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mr1cjAz2y9I)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vt_CjAdzebM)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "content";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779736467"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Input Text";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Input Text is a generic term for various types of text that require correction. It can appear in multiple contexts, such as a Sanskrit-like text that needs correction based on domain-specific terms, a transcript from a YouTube video analyzed for compliance with correction rules, or a guided meditation script containing intentional and unintentional errors. The term also applies to a string of transcription errors, exemplified by the sequence 'ülülül...', which indicates a transcription error.  

The input text may exhibit several issues, including repetitive use of the word \"critical\" and the mention of \"dheera,\" a term associated with courage and victory. It often lacks conversational filler and may contain transcription errors, mishearings, domain-specific terms, and punctuation issues. For instance, the text might feature a string of 'ülülül...' as a transcription error, or it might be a guided meditation script with both intentional and unintentional errors.  

Correction of the input text involves addressing domain-specific terms, punctuation, and the identified errors. The process follows correction rules, which may include handling intentional and unintentional errors. The goal is to ensure the text is accurate and compliant with the required standards, whether it is a Sanskrit-like text, a YouTube transcript, or a meditation script.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-62e25e090c1f38b8ad8fb3b011d0eb34<SEP>chunk-6239363e43b90d034be5850e9ec19b9d<SEP>chunk-4aa2186804f084108c45c41993118d21<SEP>chunk-32d242f8b8589873c418da28de2aa7f5<SEP>chunk-ac6391e06ee1d9f0eaf83699fa502ac7<SEP>chunk-25c321e128bae2ec1d82719bef8c6996<SEP>chunk-591036e7b8f7e9576e9f165456e4f909<SEP>chunk-55556acea804a1064101176b4fd1d907";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

