<urn:mukthiguru:Insecurity> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI)<SEP>YouTube Video: U23yKxWbIcI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U23yKxWbIcI)<SEP>YouTube Video: BZDXIQwOPdU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BZDXIQwOPdU)<SEP>YouTube Video: _GEMrEWCiXw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_GEMrEWCiXw)<SEP>YouTube Video: HELtP96Dd4w (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HELtP96Dd4w)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oZRQoiRe7s4)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-bff75bb2f7b2ca92ac4ac1a9d943c725<SEP>chunk-37c881d41553a8a7658ca326a33a2864<SEP>chunk-3ae96ad01fcb39bd7a75f6d45072f0d6<SEP>chunk-9d6f79b5d9addaa1bb7ed5a41e6ca13e<SEP>chunk-7d81041aa6a8c1ffd7fa363d2179e32d<SEP>chunk-08f2f333c27085728d7608b7e47baa48<SEP>chunk-f97c33bc1c34505752dbdf13ce792596<SEP>chunk-1a2d9f9a94f699ed87aa72d476d3870c<SEP>chunk-0cb21e09915c74bf08c75e2e9b3c1480<SEP>chunk-4be5f58baaab4360b84499e4e9c8f89b<SEP>chunk-18dfe327019b4987cc16243e45ad4a98<SEP>chunk-1049ffa49a880db4b5369cf84bcae432<SEP>chunk-5424541c24943ffc408f99bb3aa45c96<SEP>chunk-641507fc1ac65e5fc2ff612c296612f6<SEP>chunk-9f1528e052c091ff9a2052d88bff2e72<SEP>chunk-7acdb8dcc103d74a206701373f78fcb9<SEP>chunk-71c647fd13898f185a71091bf9fbd510<SEP>chunk-37a50ba57b87bf8d444df3da83283e84<SEP>chunk-428c28379181a7cdc217fc69118ccc4d";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779687750"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Insecurity is a persistent feeling of inadequacy rooted in childhood experiences, influencing relationships and behaviors, as exemplified by Mei. It is an unwise emotional state that leads to unwise actions and can sabotage intelligence. Insecurity fuels fear and hate, creating cycles of contagion across individuals and generations, and is listed among emotions underlying discriminatory behaviors and societal tensions. It is reinforced through generational narratives of division and conflict, and is an emotion resulting from discrimination, passed down through stories. Insecurity acts as a driver of fear and hate, perpetuating cycles of conflict.

Insecurity is a psychological state linked to generational trauma and discrimination. It is listed among emotional barriers that prevent individuals from experiencing or sharing love effectively. Insecurity describes a state of self-doubt and fear of inadequacy related to one's physical traits, and also a state of self-doubt or fear of inadequacy, often driving behaviors like cosmetic procedures. Insecurity is a contributing factor to internal conflict and resulting stress.

These aspects collectively illustrate how insecurity operates across personal, relational, and societal levels, shaping behaviors and perpetuating negative cycles.<SEP>Insecurity is a concept that oscillates with security.`<SEP>Insecurity refers to a lack of self-confidence that often manifests in relationships as distrust or overthinking.<SEP>Insecurity involves self-doubt that can manifest as excessive need for validation or control in relationships.<SEP>Insecurity involves self-doubt that can manifest as excessive need for validation or control in relationships.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Insecurity" .

