<urn:mukthiguru:Intention> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Intention";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Intention is a concept that reflects the beneficiary of a decision, encompassing both self-interest and collective benefit. It is described as a subtle power that influences decisions, determining who benefits from them. Intention also reflects the beneficiary of a decision and its impact on well-being and others, indicating its broader social and personal implications.

Intention is a goal-oriented aspect of energy flow, shaped by the interplay of chaos and order. This perspective frames intention as a dynamic force that can direct outcomes, especially when combined with conscious states.

However, intention alone is deemed insufficient for achieving longevity without action. It is a focused mental directive used in conjunction with conscious states to actualize desired outcomes, such as destiny creation. Thus, while intention provides direction and purpose, it must be coupled with deliberate action to realize its full potential.<SEP>A focused mental directive used in conjunction with conscious states to actualize desired outcomes like destiny creation.<SEP>A focused mental directive used in conjunction with conscious states to actualize desired outcomes like destiny creation.<SEP>Holding an intention, which is part of creating a magical destiny.<SEP>Holding an intention, which is part of creating a magical destiny.<SEP>Intention refers to the act of making intentions manifest as part of the soul sync process.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779728642"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
