<urn:mukthiguru:Interview> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching from the contaminated text. The contaminated text includes both the real content and some developer instructions.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The descriptions mention \"Interview\" as a scenario for entering Oneness, free from stress, connecting with universal intelligence, and enabling healing. The core elements are Oneness, stress-free consciousness, universal intelligence, and outcomes like healing and extraordinary responses.

The developer parts are the instructions on how to structure the summary, the plan with paragraphs, and the token count. I need to remove all that. The key is to present the spiritual concept in 1-4 sentences without any bullet points or headers.

Looking at the long description, the main points are the state of Oneness, connection to universal intelligence, and the outcomes. The short descriptions reinforce these points. The variations in emphasis are noted but don't affect the core message.

So, the clean description should mention Interview as a transformative experience where one enters Oneness, connects with universal intelligence, and achieves healing through connected consciousness. I need to make sure it's concise, in plain English, and only includes the spiritual aspects without any extra instructions or formatting.
</think>

Interview is a transformative spiritual experience where one enters a state of Oneness, free from mental and emotional stress, and connects with universal intelligence. In this state, connected consciousness enables extraordinary responses and relationship healing. Descriptions of Interview vary in emphasis—some focus on core elements like Oneness and stress-free consciousness, while others highlight outcomes such as healing and extraordinary communication. These variations reflect different levels of elaboration but consistently underscore Interview’s unified nature as a spiritual process merging deep connection with transformative communication.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Interview";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-8a1bd6015acf3ec9471eb585d90f59e5<SEP>chunk-0218062ded6a8b7c8b783d92c65d1917";
