<urn:mukthiguru:Jaya> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-749e889c128e710cc18adc38c4d377cb<SEP>chunk-0e0d8ce525e6e00265646821c7a82b74<SEP>chunk-abf598569eb5f03bc21c09bf7af4abf7<SEP>chunk-c0eee090a2741e82903b80d77573da86<SEP>chunk-dd609ab9c79e0fc5514db3c901de7f50<SEP>chunk-ba4ba0d6f181ef0bbd4fc17f6bc9ea4d<SEP>chunk-25634a7e16db511e9e5b4a8597da99fd<SEP>chunk-697da9f4d9cac1cfedd243857a8b8ccc<SEP>chunk-0e5b03097ca1fd70284be6d33317832d<SEP>chunk-da0dcd44b642ae88bb5ae6bfa953a323";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Jaya is a person who experienced a traumatic childhood marked by abuse and poverty. She endured the abuse, ran away from home at the age of twelve, and later recontextualized her trauma as a source of empowerment, using storytelling and team motivation to shape her narrative. Despite these efforts, she maintains a successful career, leveraging her experiences to drive her professional achievements.

Jaya is driven by a deep-seated anger and an intense need to prove herself, which leads her to mask her childhood pain and construct an outward image of independence. This defensive posture leaves her struggling with unresolved emotional wounds, making it difficult for her to trust or form intimate relationships.

Jaya undergoes a personal metamorphosis, during which she metaphorically describes her childhood as radioactive waste emitting harmful radiation in her mind. She grapples with emotional connection, discipline, and workplace relationships, which culminate in employee turnover and personal isolation. Her rage, bitterness, and difficulty in trust further exacerbate these challenges.

Overall, Jaya's life reflects a complex interplay between past trauma and present coping mechanisms. While she has achieved professional success and attempts to transform her pain into empowerment, she continues to confront inner struggles with emotional connection, self-awareness, and the lingering effects of her early experiences.<SEP>Jaya is a self-made individual who struggles with emotional connections, viewing love as a weakness and maintaining unresolved resentment toward her mother. She disciplines her children but lacks emotional intimacy, and her workplace conflicts lead to high employee turnover.<SEP>Jaya is a person who endured an abusive childhood, built a successful career, and later realized her inner turmoil stemmed from unresolved trauma.` - This is a good summary.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779183757"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Jaya";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person" .

