  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Life after death is a belief held by multiple cultures, including Egyptians and early Christians.<SEP>Life after death was treated as factual in ancient philosophy, not mythical.`<SEP>Life after death refers to the continuation of existence beyond physical death, a theme in various spiritual traditions.<SEP>Life after death is a philosophical and religious concept debated across cultures, including Egyptian civilization, Judaism, and Christianity.<SEP>Life after death is a belief in continued existence beyond physical death, discussed in religious contexts.<SEP>Life After Death is a philosophical concept central to multiple traditions, including Egyptian, Jewish, and Christian beliefs.";
