  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Life standards refer to the overall quality of living conditions experienced by individuals or groups. According to the provided descriptions, life standards are improving physically, indicating progress in areas such as health, nutrition, and material resources. However, these improvements are accompanied by a lag in social and emotional well‑being, suggesting that while material conditions are advancing, aspects of mental health, social cohesion, and emotional support are not keeping pace.

The increase in life standards is attributed to enhanced access to basic goods and services, which are contributing to the physical improvements. Overall, the picture of life standards is mixed: physical and material aspects are on an upward trajectory, whereas social and emotional dimensions remain relatively stagnant.<SEP>Life standards are noted to be improving physically but lagging in social/emotional well-being.""" .

