<urn:mukthiguru:Longevity%20Genes> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Longevity Genes";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Longevity Genes are genetic traits that enable humans to live longer. According to multiple descriptions, these genetic factors are associated with evolutionary advantages that arise from caring for grandchildren. The traits also support intergenerational support and contribute to species survival. The consistency across the provided descriptions indicates a well-established link between longevity genes and these evolutionary benefits.

The concept of longevity genes highlights how genetic variations can promote extended lifespan, which in turn fosters behaviors that enhance the survival of offspring and grandchildren. This intergenerational support is viewed as an adaptive strategy that benefits the broader species. The repeated emphasis on caring for grandchildren across the descriptions underscores the evolutionary significance of these genetic traits.

The provided descriptions are consistent, indicating a coherent understanding of longevity genes and their evolutionary implications.<SEP>Genetic traits enabling humans to live longer are linked to evolutionary advantages in caring for grandchildren.<SEP>Genetic factors in humans that enable extended lifespan, linked to intergenerational support and species survival.<SEP>Longevity genes are hypothetical biological mechanisms associated with extended lifespan and healthspan.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-b2b3f4e0ec4ca323c0c90b860c94bdb5<SEP>chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef<SEP>chunk-7438d62acfd111c95d021226c6581819";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779656853"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

