  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Mahal-e-amavasya is a ritual dedicated to appeasing ancestors who died in unhappy conditions.`<SEP>Mahal-e-amavasya is a day dedicated to appeasing the spirits of ancestors who may have passed away in unhappy conditions or undesirable conditions.<SEP>Mahal-e-amavasya refers to a lunar eclipse event in Islamic tradition, associated with spiritual significance.<SEP>Mahal-e-amavasya is a special new moon day observed by Koreans to honor ancestors and release departed souls.<SEP>Mahal-e-amavasya is a day dedicated to appeasing the spirits of ancestors who died in unhappy conditions.<SEP>Mahal-e-amavasya is a Korean special new moon day to honor ancestors and release departed souls in suffering." .

<urn:mukthiguru:Mahalakshmi> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-999724134081683327acbc7368915cf5<SEP>chunk-7dcda87b32c6120a6328a9d38eb2e300<SEP>chunk-cdb7e2c2a992ab4d052399a789ce199f<SEP>chunk-672a64891a721958057240b2cc83a897<SEP>chunk-49d819fbab36af31ec15419ab94d1279<SEP>chunk-7b3a64aa7e92b879d5649be1dd23a938<SEP>chunk-a7efc3b9dab03e6e433daab7a3b11310<SEP>chunk-0ab03500cfe03bdf3ff37b159be99afe<SEP>chunk-3d108a7609d2fce897a3df1f09942814<SEP>chunk-0d847b42bbc0f3e13f07c034a5c8e0d1";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V5fBJwo_KQk)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: WfkCDNu4SuE (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WfkCDNu4SuE)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jy4hcpUSBms)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Mahalakshmi is a Hindu goddess revered as the Divine Mother, embodying wealth, abundance, and prosperity. She is also associated with the concept of transcending Rajas, symbolizing the overcoming of incessant desire. Mahalakshmi is a central figure in the Navratri festival, though traditions vary regarding which days of the festival she is most prominently worshipped. Some accounts associate her with the later days (days 7-9), others with the fourth to sixth days, and still others with the middle days. This diversity reflects differing regional and sectarian practices.

During the Mahalakshmi Upasana ritual, she is depicted with specific iconographic attributes, which are integral to her worship. The goddess is invoked for blessings and abundance, and her role as the Mother Goddess is emphasized in devotional contexts. Mahalakshmi's association with the middle days of Navaratri is particularly noted for her symbolism of prosperity and the transcendence of Rajas.

In summary, Mahalakshmi is a multifaceted deity who combines the attributes of wealth, abundance, and the Divine Mother, while also representing the spiritual transcendence of Rajas. Her worship spans various days of Navratri, with traditions differing on the specific timing, and she is honored through specific iconographic representations during rituals. This synthesis captures the essential aspects of Mahalakshmi as described in the provided accounts.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Mahalakshmi";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779673531"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

