<urn:mukthiguru:Mahatma%20Gandhi> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-42e3465bd48ea87621d94e9d33063209<SEP>chunk-37e9823f1b7627730cb977ca684bcc4a<SEP>chunk-3315cd2e438010dca35a1192e534e125<SEP>chunk-dec047b5cab8e88110c88f8cc2cfcd7d<SEP>chunk-0c3de714c4e42df4c68c8fd79dfac5ad<SEP>chunk-dbf66e2de209f9688955866d38e39e63<SEP>chunk-54ab0057ebb9d14ac4c0eb525f843612";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Mahatma Gandhi (meaning \"the Great Soul\") symbolizes the embodiment of nonviolent resistance and oppressed peoples' victory.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi was a leader who guided India to independence from British rule through non-violent resistance.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi is referenced as having a historic brush with inner truth.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi is the title given to Gandhi, meaning \"the Great Soul,\" and he is a key influencer in human history.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi, originally Gandhi, is a historical figure transformed into a symbol of nonviolent resistance and spiritual greatness after his awakening to inner truth.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi is a key influencer in human history, associated with nonviolence and the victory of the weak over oppressors.<SEP>Mahatma Gandhi led India to independence through nonviolent resistance rooted in compassion rather than personal hatred.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
