  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Mallory is an individual who appears in the narrative and is addressed by the speaker. The speaker repeatedly refers to Mallory as a “capella beautiful mirror,” a phrase that suggests a pure, unaccompanied beauty. Seven out of eight descriptions align with this characterization, indicating that the speaker’s view of Mallory is as a pristine, self-contained mirror of beauty. However, one description diverges by adding a dimension of self-awareness to Mallory’s portrayal, presenting her as both a reflective, self-aware entity and a pure, unaccompanied mirror of beauty. Together, these perspectives present Mallory as a complex figure who embodies both inner reflection and aesthetic qualities.<SEP>Mallory is an individual addressed by the speaker, described as a \"capella beautiful mirror.\"<SEP>Mallory is an individual addressed by the speaker, described as a \"capella beautiful mirror.\"<SEP>Mallory is an individual addressed by the speaker, described as a \"capella beautiful mirror.\"<SEP>Mallory is an individual addressed by the speaker, described as a \"capella beautiful mirror.\"";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779518077"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Mallory" .

