- Marriage as a social institution and human institution representing partnership and commitment.
- Subject to societal and cultural frameworks, historically and culturally governed, discussed in context of evolving values.
- Examined within broader context of societal constructs and existential priorities.
- In India, marriage is portrayed as an institution facing societal and parental pressures regarding its success criteria.
- Marriage is considered a significant life event, particularly in the context of spiritual practices.

Also note that the short description repeats: \"Marriage is mentioned as a significant life event in the context of spiritual practices.\" So we can incorporate that as a concise statement.

