\"Meditation Practice is a method that involves conscious breathing and focusing on universal intelligence. It encompasses a variety of techniques, including breath control, chanting, and body awareness. Practitioners often observe breath cycles, maintain focus, and achieve thought coherence through guided breathing exercises. Some forms of meditation practice incorporate the chanting of the Ekam mantra to foster unity with family and the divine. Sustained meditation practice has been shown to reverse the dominance of the limbic system over the prefrontal cortex in the brain. Additionally, meditation practice involves focused attention and repetition to rewire neural pathways, reducing amygdala activity and enhancing prefrontal cortex function. These changes contribute to greater thought coherence and overall mental well‑being.\"

