- It is fundamentally composed of thoughts.
- It is the central element of human consciousness and cognitive processes.
- It underpins perception and interaction.
- It experiences 15k-60k thoughts per day.
- It is expressed through metaphors: cart, train, narrow lane.
- In meditation, it is part of the mind-body connection.
- It is the seat of consciousness, unconscious processes, and mental states.
- It has both aware and non-aware aspects.

