<urn:mukthiguru:Money> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oUCZWSi8zY4)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: oXRZhJTHuOA (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oXRZhJTHuOA)<SEP>YouTube Video: vjEsXpEtpH4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vjEsXpEtpH4)<SEP>YouTube Video: 2seBB2oByZc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2seBB2oByZc)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Money is an entity that functions as a material manifestation of wealth, vulnerable to depletion, and serves as a medium of exchange and economic value. It is a tangible representation of economic value and security, frequently scavenged to fill personal voids, and plays a role in community and individual decision-making. Money also acts as a determinant of social behavior and resource access, influencing how individuals and groups interact and allocate resources. Beyond its economic functions, Money symbolizes wealth and economic power, evoking complex emotional and psychological responses. It is a material concept examined in relation to human desires and existential significance, reflecting deeper meanings beyond mere utility. Money is highlighted as a determinant of social behavior and resource access, and it represents economic resources that play a role in community and individual decision-making.

In certain cultural contexts, Money is related to the act of making a son, indicating symbolic or social associations. This relation underscores the multifaceted nature of Money, which is not only a material and economic entity but also a cultural and symbolic one. Money's role in decision-making and its impact on social behavior further illustrate its pervasive influence across various domains. Money is a material manifestation of wealth that can be depleted, highlighting its finite nature, and it serves as a medium of exchange and economic value, shaping how individuals and groups interact and allocate resources.<SEP>Money represents economic resources that play a role in community and individual decision-making.<SEP>Money is highlighted as a determinant of social behavior and resource access.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-7f167e0e6ad11f51a72e88b506b459a9<SEP>chunk-fdd895baa3282f9ed911c72eae7a3d65<SEP>chunk-9233fc2d9357336158890082052af34c<SEP>chunk-407afcc34149e3cdc533c3a522a0ac53<SEP>chunk-075b8e71a3c71d11c785be4bbfe965ed<SEP>chunk-a9f29aa70d2aed842238204adf8a81c5<SEP>chunk-25f394f47fe40575ea9fbcd110df6414<SEP>chunk-9eea478f3eb12a678ce672d3075c4af8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Money";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779551879"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

