<urn:mukthiguru:Monkeys> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Monkeys are mischievous creatures targeted by villagers using a trapping method involving desserts and tree hollows.<SEP>Monkeys are burly, mischievous creatures that steal from homes and are trapped using a method involving desserts.<SEP>The monkeys represent obstacles and fears that Swami Vivekananda confronts, illustrating the theme of overcoming challenges.<SEP>Mischievous monkeys that steal from homes and get trapped by villagers using desserts as bait.<SEP>Monkeys are animals referenced in comparisons highlighting reduced human attention spans due to technological distractions.<SEP>Monkeys are referenced as having greater attention spans than human beings in the context of modern technological distractions.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-bb336118db8922490b3e05a79c11dba1<SEP>chunk-b0b6f9f02020768407fee531e6074a4d<SEP>chunk-379dcbaa1fba64cd1d562fe797bdcf77<SEP>chunk-71a9fb4bfe84373a489e9a88ded57dae<SEP>chunk-f0801bcd006400c8824a3d4098716493<SEP>chunk-1b2894d7e044a8fc57ea102bdd508b16<SEP>chunk-d89831c29a65e71a84017ad0bb3212c4";
