- It is characterized by freedom from suffering, illusion, cycle of rebirth (Samsara), conflict-driven minds.
- It is one of the four pursuits (likely in some tradition, maybe Buddhist or Hindu).
- It can be pursued through spiritual seeking.
- In the \"Nobody State\", spiritual seeking becomes ambitious/aggressive, leading to an aggressive pursuit of knowledge for display rather than genuine enlightenment.
- In the \"Beautiful State\", spiritual seeking evolves into knowledge for genuine liberation.
- Mukti signifies freedom from the cycle of Samsara and realization of ultimate truth.
- It is also described as liberation from ego-driven states, emphasizing peaceful coexistence.
- It is associated with peacefulness, immense peacefulness.

We need to integrate all.

