<urn:mukthiguru:Narrator> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Narrator";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779518302"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-e5fa2d640a5c60cb68e25b39b952c1d0<SEP>chunk-03f4910a466e54c3db3456e161f19c10<SEP>chunk-9924c7e219f96915a4ef19eba2cb5f62<SEP>chunk-ad886d6b8bed920b247267424ac5e9aa<SEP>chunk-c85036006eb9517f84fbb3ee7717030e<SEP>chunk-aa9fb91dec3c3871071d93754b61c5e8<SEP>chunk-cde14d696f27021b8bd46431e4e80d28<SEP>chunk-00283c6d3847e844c97d2dea1db37c97<SEP>chunk-e48cb770a294a3d305875880cc43095f<SEP>chunk-95ede5878070f28d1b63e5213e0a1f6e<SEP>chunk-84c6a3d9c8b4cde9bffa20b37bd7d9c0<SEP>chunk-ef58d1ac43cade418f738ee9bfcca18c<SEP>chunk-338cfb2aa25fb2dee64396603e703b28<SEP>chunk-aaeba0a2e3dac75ac3bf2d72063fa0eb<SEP>chunk-0e0d394b4b504c272b6565228b821607";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: y2ZgKdt4Cj0 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y2ZgKdt4Cj0)<SEP>YouTube Video: ds6FM6QEDWM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ds6FM6QEDWM)<SEP>YouTube Video: YguId6pF5KI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YguId6pF5KI)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Narrator is a multifaceted figure characterized by inherited visions, shared consciousness, and frustration over instructional failures. In some accounts, the narrator experiences anger, self‑reflection, and eventually realizes that self‑centric thinking is the root of suffering. The narrator also demonstrates an empathic connection, perceiving others’ emotions as if they were one’s own, and describes this connection as a natural state of being. Additionally, the narrator reflects on personal relationships, including marriage and emotional experiences with Krishnaji and their daughter, as well as broader familial dynamics. In another context, the narrator recounts an accident, receives help from a compassionate woman, and reflects on the nature of right action and its link to spontaneous compassion. Finally, the narrator undergoes intense self‑reflection, anger, and ultimately attains enlightenment regarding the nature of suffering and self‑centric thinking.<SEP>Narrator is the speaker reflecting on spiritual vision and its impact on life experiences, contrasting it with goal-oriented thinking.<SEP>The storyteller who engages the gentleman in dialogue, offering insights on gratitude and self-awareness.<SEP>The narrator is a person reflecting on their relationship with their daughter and attending the Field of Abundance event with their father.<SEP>The Narrator describes personal experiences of heightened consciousness and spiritual awakening, including timeless states and dissolution of self-identity.<SEP>The narrator is a person who developed a transformational teaching method after participating in OCLC programs, aiming to help others overcome suffering." .

<urn:mukthiguru:Nation> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-0cb21e09915c74bf08c75e2e9b3c1480<SEP>chunk-89ab86758e55eda4e32bf5581a61d209<SEP>chunk-e22181d45ff680a216a2e1e3bb46c19d";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """The Nation is a term that can refer to the collective identity and interests of a country's people. It can also be used in the plural to describe societal consciousness states, ranging from division to unity.

In some contexts, the term may be capitalized when referring to a specific entity, but as a general concept it should be lowercase. Additionally, the Nation is sometimes urged to confront its own prejudices and enter a 'crucible of truth' for societal change.<SEP>Nation refers to the collective identity and interests of a country's people.<SEP>Nation refers to the collective identity and interests of a country's people.<SEP>Nation refers to the collective identity and interests of a country's people.<SEP>Nation refers to the collective identity and interests of a country's people.<SEP>Nation refers to the collective identity and interests of a country's people.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779719904"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Nation";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kPuvsIyt6UI)<SEP>YouTube Video: _GEMrEWCiXw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_GEMrEWCiXw)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=77dJnbTCwsA)" .

