  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Negative Emotions include anger, shame, stress, and worry, which the text warns against misusing as motivation.<SEP>Negative emotions are discussed as potential sources of dependency and suffering.<SEP>Emotions such as hurt, disappointment, loneliness, anger, and anxiety that dominate when disappointments and longings are unaddressed.<SEP>Negative emotions are caused by habits and can be observed.<SEP>Negative emotions like anger, fear, and sadness are habitual states that impact human behavior and decision-making.<SEP>Negative emotions arise from mental movies about the past and future, and the amygdala is the brain region that feeds on these emotions.<SEP>Emotional states like fear and anxiety, which are triggered by the amygdala." .

