<urn:mukthiguru:Omega%20Energy> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Omega Energy";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-ad2ebfd9c09b89878454033624d3cb86<SEP>chunk-559fad8d464d0831db20c5c057d17eb5<SEP>chunk-7248fb4a5efc0d07c14a1dfefd59324e<SEP>chunk-a0501780b62546f91638cd76288d70a0<SEP>chunk-d1911383179e65a76d16c03a5d5707f5<SEP>chunk-5c68b9015fbb59203618736e8841a1fe<SEP>chunk-1e7e55f43ce6e8842a2479ee424af0b9<SEP>chunk-059ace20f2db1cc39262846db5c238d9";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices. This increase reflects the company's exposure to the energy sector and its sensitivity to commodity price fluctuations. The stock's upward movement is directly linked to the rising oil prices, which have positively impacted the company's market valuation. Investors and analysts view this as a positive indicator of the company's performance under current market conditions.

The repeated descriptions of Omega Energy in the provided list consistently report the same stock performance, reinforcing the reliability of this information. The company's identity as an energy firm is central to understanding why oil price changes affect its stock value.

The stock's performance is a direct result of the broader energy market dynamics, where oil price trends significantly influence investor sentiment and valuation. This relationship underscores the importance of monitoring commodity prices for stakeholders in the energy sector.<SEP>Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices.`<SEP>Omega Energy is an energy company that gained 2.1% in stock value due to rising oil prices.`""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=obK5uqYXOJU)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "organization";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779748722"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

