  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and some actual content about Ono.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual teachings or concepts. The contaminated text mentions that Ono is a place name, possibly a mishearing of \"One,\" associated with spirituality in business, and a location the user visited. The key points are the ambiguity, the mishearing, and the connection to spirituality in business teachings.

I should remove all the developer instructions like \"We need to synthesize...\" or \"We must handle conflicts...\" and focus on the actual content. The example output provided by the user starts with \"Ono is a place name...\" and includes the mishearing, ambiguity, and the spiritual aspects. I need to make sure the output is concise, in plain English, and within 1-4 sentences without any bullet points or headers.

Looking at the example, they combined the points into two paragraphs. The first introduces Ono as a place name with possible mishearing and ambiguity. The second mentions the location visited and the spirituality in business teachings. I should follow that structure but ensure it's clean and only includes the necessary information without any extra details from the instructions.

Also, check if there's any mention of the user's spiritual journey. The contaminated text says \"linked to the user's spiritual journey,\" so that should be included. Make sure the output is objective and third-person, avoiding any personal pronouns. Finally, ensure the total is under 600 tokens, but since the example is short, that's probably covered.
</think>

Ono is a place name that may be a mishearing of \"One\" and functions as a proper noun with ambiguous origins. It is described as a location associated with spirituality in business, where teachings on spiritual principles within business contexts were explored. The entity appears in the context of a user's spiritual journey, linking physical""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Ono";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "location" .

