<urn:mukthiguru:Original%20Meaning> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Original Meaning";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779735302"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Original Meaning is a concept that the original meaning of a chant is often garbled and repetitive, requiring correction to align with the author's intended meaning. This perspective highlights that the original meaning is not to be retained absolutely, but rather functions as a constraint during the correction process.

Original Meaning is also described as a constraint that should not be retained absolutely. Multiple descriptions emphasize that the original meaning serves as a constraint, and one view specifically notes that during corrections one must avoid retaining the original non-existent meaning. In practice, this means that while the original meaning may be flawed, it should not be preserved as an absolute truth; instead, corrections should aim to reflect the author's intended meaning, and any attempt to retain the original meaning must be avoided to prevent perpetuating a non-existent interpretation.<SEP>Constraint requiring avoidance of retaining the original non-existent meaning during corrections.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1w-IStuMl3M)<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-1439496c0597ca312586a923b138c34d<SEP>chunk-3718c86a25fb0b5558d0d13c8bf954d4<SEP>chunk-24979790543830f1142942642c3d852a" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Original%20Meaning%20Preservation> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779700971"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-5eced850d74f972c1d65bf6b3ae924fd<SEP>chunk-7fd8596e77267f333f42ebc055048d2e";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Original Meaning Preservation is a constraint that governs how corrections are applied to a text. It requires that any modifications retain the original meaning, prohibiting the introduction of new ideas, the removal of existing content, the addition of interpretations, and the rewriting of style. By preserving the author's intent and the factual and stylistic elements of the original text, this constraint ensures that edits align with the intended message without altering the tone or shifting the meaning.

In practice, Original Meaning Preservation guides editors and proofreaders to make minimal changes that keep the text faithful to its source, maintaining the integrity of the original communication. The principle is applied across various editorial contexts, where it serves as a guiding rule for making the smallest possible adjustments that correct errors while staying true to the original author's voice.

This approach prevents the distortion of the text's core message and ensures that any revisions are transparent and justifiable, thereby upholding the authenticity of the original work. The constraint is succinctly defined as requiring corrections to retain the original meaning without adding interpretations or rewriting style, a concise formulation that captures the essence of the broader description.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Original Meaning Preservation";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Original%20Meaning%20Retention> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Constraint to strictly avoid altering the original philosophical meaning during corrections.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779402380"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Original Meaning Retention";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-288b6f3cbc1fbe491495841582bf9281";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: vjEsXpEtpH4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vjEsXpEtpH4)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "constraint" .

