<urn:mukthiguru:Pachamama> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content about Pachamama from the contaminated text. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and meta-information, so I need to filter that out.

First, I'll look through the contaminated text. The main points about Pachamama are spread across three descriptions. The first one mentions she's an indigenous earth mother goddess, deity, associated with aquarius flowers, linked to Gaia in lyrics, invoked in chants, embodies Earth Mother energy, and is connected to fertility, nature, cycles, harmony. The second description says she's the Earth Mother in indigenous traditions, emphasizing harmony with nature. The third adds that she's an Andean deity representing life-giving and nurturing qualities.

I need to combine these into a clean summary without any of the task instructions. The user wants it in 1-4 sentences, plain English, no bullet points or headers. Let me structure it as per the paragraphs mentioned but condense it. Start with introducing Pachamama as an Andean earth mother goddess. Then mention her associations like fertility, nature, cycles, harmony, Earth Mother energy, and her symbols like Gaia and aquarius flowers. Finally, highlight her life-giving qualities and harmony with nature. Make sure to avoid repetition and keep it concise. Check if all key points are covered: indigenous, Andean, fertility, nature, cycles, harmony, Earth Mother energy, Gaia, aquarius flowers, life-giving, nurturing. Yes, that's all there. Now, put it together smoothly without any markdown.
</think>

Pachamama is an indigenous earth mother goddess and deity in Andean traditions, symbolizing the Earth's life-giving and nurturing qualities. She embodies Earth Mother energy, representing fertility, natural cycles, and harmony with nature. Associated with aquarius flowers, she is often equated with Gaia in lyrics and invoked in ch""";
