<urn:mukthiguru:Pawn%20in%20the%20chessboard%20of%20life> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6052761888817e6a639d7d02535dd8c5";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779748651"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Pawn in the chessboard of life";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching from the contaminated text. The contaminated text has a lot of developer instructions and some repeated content.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The main points mentioned are that \"Pawn in the chessboard of life\" is a metaphor comparing life to a chessboard, with individuals as pawns. It emphasizes the structured, strategic nature of life, where each person's moves are limited but crucial, and the metaphor is accurate and appropriately written.

The contaminated text includes instructions on how to structure the summary, like using multiple paragraphs, avoiding bullet points, and keeping it under 600 tokens. But I need to ignore all that. The actual content is in the parts that describe the metaphor itself. The repeated mentions of \"the metaphor was correctly written\" are part of the key points to include.

I should combine the long and short descriptions. The long one has more details about the structured nature and strategic moves, while the short one just states it's a correctly written metaphor. The user also mentioned to avoid repetition, so I need to present the information concisely without repeating the same points multiple times.

Putting it all together, the clean description should start with the entity name, state it's a metaphor, compare life to a chessboard, mention individuals as pawns, explain the structured and strategic aspects, the limited but crucial moves, and note the metaphor's accuracy. All in plain English, 1-4 sentences, no markdown. Let me check if I missed any key points. The structured nature, strategic elements, limited moves, and the metaphor's correctness are all covered. That should be it.
</think>

Pawn in the chessboard of life is a metaphor comparing life to a chessboard, where individuals act as pawns bound by the game's rules. This metaphor highlights life's structured and strategic nature, with each person making limited yet crucial moves. The concept""" .

