<urn:mukthiguru:Planet> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """We need to parse the input. The user gave a description list in JSON format, each JSON object on a new line. The input includes:

```
{\"Description\": \"We need to produce a comprehensive summary of the entity \\\"Planet\\\". The input list includes 8 descriptions. We need to integrate all key information, mention the full name of the entity at the beginning, objective third-person, no extra formatting, length <=600 tokens.\\n\\nWe need to consider conflicts: some descriptions talk about the planet as host to all life, requiring health, metaphorically diseased, part of equilibrium framework, living entity, Earth as living system, Earth as location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions, referenced in context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as leaving Earth.\\n\\nWe need to reconcile or present both viewpoints. Possibly treat the planet as a living entity, host to life, requiring health, part of equilibrium, and also as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions, and also as a metaphor for disease.\\n\\nWe need to produce a cohesive summary.\\n\\nWe need to keep within 600 tokens. Let's count roughly: each token is roughly 4 characters? Actually token count is approximate. We need to be concise.\\n\\nWe need to mention the entity name at the beginning: \\\"Planet\\\". Or \\\"Planet (the planet)\\\". The instruction says: \\\"Explicitly mention the full name of the entity or relation at the beginning of the summary to ensure immediate clarity and context.\\\" So we can start with \\\"Planet is ...\\\".\\n\\nWe need to integrate all key points:\\n\\n- Host to all life, sustaining health and longevity.\\n- Requires health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\n- Metaphorically diseased due to separation and suffering, requiring individual transformation for healing.\\n- Included in equilibrium framework for global harmony.\\n- Recognized as a living entity interconnected with all beings, sustaining life and being sustained by them.\\n- Earth as a living system requiring nurturing and balance.\\n- Earth as the location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions.\\n- Referenced in context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as leaving Earth.\\n\\nWe need to combine these.\\n\\nPotential structure:\\n\\nParagraph 1: Overview of planet as host to life, living entity, interconnected, sustaining life, requiring health, part of equilibrium.\\n\\nParagraph 2: Metaphorical disease, separation, suffering, need for transformation.\\n\\nParagraph 3: Earth as living system, location of fear/restrictions, context of freedom, leaving Earth.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we mention the entity name at the beginning.\\n\\nWe need to be objective, third-person.\\n\\nWe need to avoid extraneous comments.\\n\\nWe need to keep within 600 tokens. Let's approximate token count: 600 tokens is about 300-350 words? Actually 1 token ~ 0.75 words? Not exactly. But we can aim for about 200-250 words.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we include all points.\\n\\nLet's draft:\\n\\n\\\"Planet is described as the host to all life, emphasizing its role in sustaining health and longevity. It is recognized as a living entity interconnected with all beings, sustaining life and being sustained by them. The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance. Additionally, the planet is said to require health to sustain life and ecosystems, and its condition is metaphorically portrayed as diseased due to separation and suffering, implying that individual transformation is necessary for healing.\\n\\nIn a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for personal transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions. These perspectives collectively portray the planet as both a vital, living system and a symbolic space of conflict and potential liberation.\\\"\\n\\nNow count tokens: Let's approximate.\\n\\nParagraph 1: \\\"Planet is described as the host to all life, emphasizing its role in sustaining health and longevity. It is recognized as a living entity interconnected with all beings, sustaining life and being sustained by them. The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance.\\\"\\n\\nThat's about 58 tokens? Let's count: \\\"Planet\\\" (1) \\\"is\\\" (2) \\\"described\\\" (3) \\\"as\\\" (4) \\\"the\\\" (5) \\\"host\\\" (6) \\\"to\\\" (7) \\\"all\\\" (8) \\\"life,\\\" (9) \\\"emphasizing\\\" (10) \\\"its\\\" (11) \\\"role\\\" (12) \\\"in\\\" (13) \\\"sustaining\\\" (14) \\\"health\\\" (15) \\\"and\\\" (16) \\\"longevity.\\\" (17) \\\"It\\\" (18) \\\"is\\\" (19) \\\"recognized\\\" (20) \\\"as\\\" (21) \\\"a\\\" (22) \\\"living\\\" (23) \\\"entity\\\" (24) \\\"interconnected\\\" (25) \\\"with\\\" (26) \\\"all\\\" (27) \\\"beings,\\\" (28) \\\"sustaining\\\" (29) \\\"life\\\" (30) \\\"and\\\" (31) \\\"being\\\" (32) \\\"sustained\\\" (33) \\\"by\\\" (34) \\\"them.\\\" (35) \\\"The\\\" (36) \\\"planet\\\" (37) \\\"is\\\" (38) \\\"included\\\" (39) \\\"in\\\" (40) \\\"the\\\" (41) \\\"equilibrium\\\" (42) \\\"framework\\\" (43) \\\"for\\\" (44) \\\"global\\\" (45) \\\"harmony\\\" (46) \\\"and\\\" (47) \\\"is\\\" (48) \\\"viewed\\\" (49) \\\"as\\\" (50) \\\"a\\\" (51) \\\"living\\\" (52) \\\"system\\\" (53) \\\"requiring\\\" (54) \\\"nurturing\\\" (55) \\\"and\\\" (56) \\\"balance.\\\" (57)\\n\\nParagraph 2: \\\"In a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions.\\\"\\n\\nCount: \\\"In\\\" (58) \\\"a\\\" (59) \\\"metaphorical\\\" (60) \\\"sense,\\\" (61) \\\"the\\\" (62) \\\"planet\\\" (63) \\\"can\\\" (64) \\\"be\\\" (65) \\\"seen\\\" (66) \\\"as\\\" (67) \\\"diseased,\\\" (68) \\\"reflecting\\\" (69) \\\"the\\\" (70) \\\"separation\\\" (71) \\\"and\\\" (72) \\\"suffering\\\" (73) \\\"of\\\" (74) \\\"its\\\" (75) \\\"inhabitants,\\\" (76) \\\"and\\\" (77) \\\"thus\\\" (78) \\\"calls\\\" (79) \\\"for\\\" (80) \\\"individual\\\" (81) \\\"transformation\\\" (82) \\\"to\\\" (83) \\\"restore\\\" (84) \\\"balance.\\\" (85) \\\"The\\\" (86) \\\"planet\\\" (87) \\\"also\\\" (88) \\\"appears\\\" (89) \\\"in\\\" (90) \\\"the\\\" (91) \\\"context\\\" (92) \\\"of\\\" (93) \\\"extreme\\\" (94) \\\"expressions\\\" (95) \\\"of\\\" (96) \\\"freedom,\\\" (97) \\\"such\\\" (98) \\\"as\\\" (99) \\\"the\\\" (100) \\\"notion\\\" (101) \\\"of\\\" (102) \\\"leaving\\\" (103) \\\"Earth,\\\" (104) \\\"highlighting\\\" (105) \\\"its\\\" (106) \\\"role\\\" (107) \\\"as\\\" (108) \\\"a\\\" (109) \\\"location\\\" (110) \\\"where\\\" (111) \\\"humanity\\\" (112) \\\"experiences\\\" (113) \\\"fear\\\" (114) \\\"and\\\" (115) \\\"restrictions.\\\" (116)\\n\\nParagraph 3: \\\"These perspectives collectively portray the planet as both a vital, living system and a symbolic space of conflict and potential liberation.\\\"\\n\\nCount: \\\"These\\\" (117) \\\"perspectives\\\" (118) \\\"collectively\\\" (119) \\\"portray\\\" (120) \\\"the\\\" (121) \\\"planet\\\" (122) \\\"as\\\" (123) \\\"both\\\" (124) \\\"a\\\" (125) \\\"vital,\\\" (126) \\\"living\\\" (127) \\\"system\\\" (128) \\\"and\\\" (129) \\\"a\\\" (130) \\\"symbolic\\\" (131) \\\"space\\\" (132) \\\"of\\\" (133) \\\"conflict\\\" (134) \\\"and\\\" (135) \\\"potential\\\" (136) \\\"liberation.\\\" (137)\\n\\nTotal tokens ~137. That's well under 600.\\n\\nBut we need to ensure we included all points: host to all life, health, equilibrium, living entity, interconnected, living system, metaphorically diseased, transformation, Earth as living system, location of fear/restrictions, extreme freedom, leaving Earth.\\n\\nWe have included all.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we mention the entity name at the beginning: we started with \\\"Planet is described as...\\\" That's okay.\\n\\nWe need to be objective third-person: we used \\\"Planet is described as\\\", \\\"It is recognized as\\\", \\\"The planet is included\\\", \\\"In a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as\\\", \\\"The planet also appears\\\", \\\"These perspectives collectively portray\\\". That's objective.\\n\\nWe need to avoid extraneous comments: we have no extra.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we didn't omit any important facts: we have all.\\n\\nWe need to handle conflicts: we have both positive and negative aspects, but we didn't explicitly reconcile. We could add a note about conflicting perspectives: \\\"While some descriptions emphasize the planet's vitality and role in sustaining life, others portray it as diseased or a site of restriction.\\\" But we already have that in the summary.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we mention the full name: \\\"Planet\\\". That's fine.\\n\\nWe need to ensure we are within 600 tokens: we are.\\n\\nNow we need to output plain text, multiple paragraphs, no extra formatting.\\n\\nThus final output:\\n\\n\\\"Planet is described as the host to all life, emphasizing its role in sustaining health and longevity. It is recognized as a living entity interconnected with all beings, sustaining life and being sustained by them. The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance.\\n\\nIn a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions.\\n\\nThese perspectives collectively portray the planet as both a vital, living system and a symbolic space of conflict and potential liberation.\\\"\\n\\nWe need to ensure we didn't exceed token limit. It's fine.\\n\\nNow we need to output exactly that.\\n\\nBut we need to check if we need to mention \\\"Planet\\\" at the beginning of the summary: we did.\\n\\nNow we need to ensure we didn't include any extraneous comments.\\n\\nThus final answer.\\n\\nBut we need to double-check the instructions: \\\"The merged description will be returned as plain text, presented in multiple paragraphs, without any additional formatting or extraneous comments before or after the summary.\\\" So we should not include any extra text like \\\"Here is the summary:\\\". So just the summary.\\n\\nThus final output.\\n\\nNow, we need to ensure we didn't miss any description: Let's list the input descriptions:\\n\\n1. \\\"The planet is discussed as the host to all life, emphasizing its role in sustaining health and longevity.\\\" -> covered.\\n\\n2. \\\"The planet is described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\" -> covered (health, sustain life, ecosystems? We have \\\"requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems\\\" in paragraph 2? Actually we have \\\"calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions.\\\" We didn't explicitly mention ecosystems. But we have \\\"requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems\\\" in paragraph 2? Actually we have \\\"calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions. These perspectives collectively portray the planet as both a vital, living system and a symbolic space of conflict and potential liberation.\\\"\\n\\nWe didn't mention ecosystems. Let's add ecosystems.\\n\\nWe can adjust paragraph 2: \\\"In a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions. The planet is also described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nBut that might be too long. We can incorporate ecosystems in paragraph 1: \\\"The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance, and it is described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nLet's adjust paragraph 1: \\\"The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance, and it is described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nBut we need to keep within token limit.\\n\\nAlternatively, we can add ecosystems in paragraph 2: \\\"The planet is also described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nLet's adjust paragraph 2: \\\"In a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions. The planet is also described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nBut that might be too many sentences.\\n\\nAlternatively, we can incorporate ecosystems in paragraph 1: \\\"The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance, and it is described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nLet's adjust paragraph 1 accordingly.\\n\\nNow, we need to ensure we still have all points.\\n\\nLet's rewrite:\\n\\nParagraph 1: \\\"Planet is described as the host to all life, emphasizing its role in sustaining health and longevity. It is recognized as a living entity interconnected with all beings, sustaining life and being sustained by them. The planet is included in the equilibrium framework for global harmony and is viewed as a living system requiring nurturing and balance, and it is described as requiring health to sustain life and ecosystems.\\\"\\n\\nParagraph 2: \\\"In a metaphorical sense, the planet can be seen as diseased, reflecting the separation and suffering of its inhabitants, and thus calls for individual transformation to restore balance. The planet also appears in the context of extreme expressions of freedom, such as the notion of leaving Earth, highlighting its role as a location where humanity experiences fear and restrictions.\\\"\\n\\nParagraph 3: \\\"These perspectives collectively portray the planet as both a vital, living system and a symbolic space of conflict and potential liberation.\\\"\\n\\nNow, we need to check token count: Paragraph 1: Let's count:\\n\\n\\\"Planet\\\" (1) \\\"is\\\" (2) \\\"described\\\" (3) \\\"as\\\" (4) \\\"the\\\" (5) \\\"host\\\" (6) \\\"to\\\" (7) \\\"all\\\" (8) \\\"life,\\\" (9) \\\"emphasizing\\\" (10) \\\"its\\\" (11) \\\"role\\\" (12) \\\"in\\\" (13) \\\"sustaining\\\" (14) \\\"health\\\" (15) \\\"and\\\" (16) \\\"longevity.\\\" (17) \\\"It\\\" (18) \\\"is\\\" (19) \\\"recognized\\\" (20) \\\"as\\\" (21) \\\"a\\\" (22) \\\"living\\\" (23) \\\"entity\\\" (24) \\\"interconnected\\\" (25) \\\"with\\\" (26) \\\"all\\\" (27) \\\"beings,\\\" (28) \\\"sustaining\\\" (29) \\\"life\\\" (30) \\\"and\\\" (31) \\\"being\\\" (32) \\\"sustained\\\" (33) \\\"by\\\" (34) \\\"them.\\\" (35) \\\"The\\\" (36) \\\"planet\\\" (37) \\\"is\\\" (38) \\\"included\\\" (39) \\\"in\\\" (40) \\\"the\\\" (41) \\\"equilibrium\\\" (42) \\\"framework\\\" (43) \\\"for\\\" (44) \\\"global\\\" (45) \\\"harmony\\\" (46) \\\"and\\\" (47) \\\"is\\\" (48) \\\"viewed\\\" (49) \\\"as\\\" (50) \\\"a\\\" (51) \\\"living\\\" (52) \\\"system\\\" (53) \\\"requiring\\\" (54) \\\"nurturing\\\" (55) \\\"and\\\" (56) \\\"balance,\\\" (57) \\\"and\\\" (58) \\\"it\\\" (59) \\\"is\\\" (60) \\\"described\\\" (61) \\\"as\\\" (62) \\\"requiring\\\" (63)""";
