<urn:mukthiguru:Pleasure> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8mmungGgDNw)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 3WnNyhhB_4w (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3WnNyhhB_4w)<SEP>YouTube Video: nCkbv_lvFfg (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nCkbv_lvFfg)<SEP>YouTube Video: ajMAwlKh3YM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajMAwlKh3YM)<SEP>YouTube Video: HELtP96Dd4w (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HELtP96Dd4w)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Pleasure";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779661692"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Pleasure is a multifaceted concept that is described in several ways across the provided descriptions. It is characterized as an addictive behavior emphasized in modern civilization, a shared human experience that highlights the undivided nature of humanity, and a fleeting, momentary experience often conflated with love but distinct from its deeper emotional and spiritual dimensions. Additionally, pleasure is described as a small part of love, distinct from the deeper connection of love, and as a pleasurable state where the illusory ego feels bloated, superior, or important.

In terms of its nature, pleasure is consistently portrayed as a fleeting, momentary experience. It is associated with dopamine-driven mechanisms and is linked to romantic love, yet it is considered a small component of deeper love. Some descriptions note that pleasure can be conflated with love, but it is distinct from love's deeper emotional and spiritual dimensions. The experience is described as fleeting and momentary, and it can lead to feelings of superiority and importance due to the bloated ego.

Pleasure also holds a significant role in modern civilization, where it is emphasized as an addictive behavior. It is identified as the fundamental essence of romantic love that drives most of humanity. This perspective views pleasure as the core of romantic love, which is a powerful force in human life. However, it is also noted that pleasure is a small part of love, and that love itself has a deeper connection that goes beyond the fleeting experience of pleasure.

The concept of pleasure includes a paradoxical aspect: it is both a fleeting, dopamine-driven experience and a state where the illusory ego feels bloated, superior, or important. Some descriptions highlight that pleasure can be conflated with love but is distinct from its deeper dimensions. Others emphasize that pleasure is the fundamental essence of romantic love, while still acknowledging that it is a small component of love. This dual nature reflects the complexity of pleasure as both a momentary experience and a driving force in human relationships.<SEP>Pleasure is a fleeting, dopamine-driven experience associated with romantic love but considered a small component of deeper love.<SEP>Pleasure is distinguished from love, described as a transient desire unrelated to love's enduring nature.<SEP>Pleasure is distinguished from love, described as a transient desire unrelated to love's enduring nature.<SEP>Pleasure is a concept that oscillates with disappointment.`""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-afded1563688b8ea6c18ff58fee20328<SEP>chunk-38cc24446242038f9819315d8c8098ea<SEP>chunk-30e3bfda839778033ca7e4ddfabb670b<SEP>chunk-811e6c42c9ccf4bfac70459d1ccf2336<SEP>chunk-beeabf4db9d94499feff9e07a340c9a1<SEP>chunk-289fa3c790540a34a24858f5f191d9ca<SEP>chunk-2d8b862305b33bd0f79f0f3bd76e8c3a<SEP>chunk-3198061b7d9cb7c891cdfe291494700c<SEP>chunk-463088ccb7af0ca596d7f4a288f68a78<SEP>chunk-1d477f5607ac5cfb56e2b711bd58f1aa<SEP>chunk-71c647fd13898f185a71091bf9fbd510" .

