<urn:mukthiguru:Polar%20Bears> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Polar Bears";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Polar Bears are a distinct group of animals, repeatedly highlighted in the input text for their unique characteristics. As a collective, they are recognized for their significance and the recurring emphasis on their role in the ecosystem. The descriptions consistently portray them as a group with notable attributes, setting them apart from other animal groups.

The input text attributes to Polar Bears a range of emotional characteristics, including feelings and wants toward newborns. They are described as having emotional states and motivations specifically related to newborn offspring. This capacity for feelings and purposeful drives toward newborns underscores their complex behavioral profile. The descriptions emphasize that these emotional traits are central to understanding their behavior and interactions.

Polar Bears exhibit a complex behavioral profile, marked by affective states and purposeful drives, particularly concerning newborn care. The input text repeatedly notes their emotional characteristics and wants toward newborns, highlighting their significance as a distinct animal group. These attributes, including their capacity for feelings and motivations, contribute to their overall behavioral complexity and make them a subject of focused attention in the descriptions.<SEP>Polar Bears are another group of animals mentioned in the input text, noted for having emotions and wants towards newborns.<SEP>Polar Bears are another group of animals mentioned in the input text, noted for having emotions and wants towards newborns.<SEP>Arctic animals referenced in the original sentences as subjects experiencing pain.<SEP>Polar bears are animals mentioned in the sentence as examples.<SEP>Polar Bears are animals mentioned in the corrected text.<SEP>Polar Bears are animals mentioned in the corrected text.""";
