  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Prejudice is addressed as external voices that individuals must reject to achieve self-acceptance. It involves preconceived opinions or discriminatory attitudes, often manifesting as color-based remarks or behaviors. Prejudice involves voices that should not be owned as one's own views, denoting preconceived judgments that obstruct objective understanding of others, and refers to preconceived opinions or biases that distort objective judgment and harm relationships.

Prejudice is tied to separation, representing judgment and division against love's unity. It is not the opposite of love but the separation from it, as described.

Prejudice is characterized by negative attitudes or judgments toward individuals perceived as different, rooted in societal divisions. It is absorbed from generations and flowing into individuals, leading to societal issues and requiring conscious realization to end.

Prejudice is a concept mentioned in the context of America's need for oneness.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: l6svaRx35TI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l6svaRx35TI)<SEP>YouTube Video: QAnRefsK-3Y (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QAnRefsK-3Y)<SEP>YouTube Video: nUrc8O7Avvk (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nUrc8O7Avvk)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XMzZe5aEmTo)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FP5O9F9JiOk)" .

