  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text. The contaminated text has a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed in. My job is to sift through that and pull out only the real spiritual teachings or definitions about Prithais.

First, I need to look at the descriptions provided. The first few points mention that Prithais is a name requiring verification or a transliteration. Then there are mentions of being a spiritual figure associated with oneness and consciousness. Other points talk about human awakening, collaboration, co-creating collective awakening and unity, and being part of a video's vision.

The challenge is to reconcile these conflicting descriptions. The key here is to identify the spiritual aspects. The name verification and transliteration parts are more about the name's status rather than spiritual content. The spiritual elements are the mentions of oneness, consciousness, human awakening, collaboration, collective awakening, unity, and being part of a video's vision related to awakening.

I need to combine these spiritual elements into a coherent description. The name Prithais is associated with these concepts. The fact that the name appears in different contexts (text scan, video) is part of the context but not the spiritual teaching itself. The main spiritual teachings are the themes of oneness, consciousness, awakening, collaboration, and unity.

So, the clean description should mention Prithais as a spiritual figure linked to these concepts, emphasizing the themes without the meta-instructions. I need to present this in 1-4 sentences, plain English, no bullet points or headers. Let me structure that.
</think>

Prithais is a spiritual figure associated with discussions of oneness, consciousness, and collective awakening. Emphasizing human collaboration and unity, Prithais co-creates visions of shared spiritual growth, often linked to themes of transcendence and interconnectedness. The name appears across multiple contexts, sometimes noted""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-78cb1d01fca05b7af18da689512d7623<SEP>chunk-4ab60e8c0bf5f4ad482e319114c89b2e<SEP>chunk-cb58e055a049ad330cf62961e6ace3a0<SEP>chunk-c7acaad240d059f10b98d44f2fbe69ce<SEP>chunk-1756c3e8d7e9eefbffb3f49a179b77fc<SEP>chunk-d319e7ca1c821b8d3953f9189c7b08fd";
