<urn:mukthiguru:Problem> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: XFFgRTgP8Rs (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XFFgRTgP8Rs)<SEP>YouTube Video: Lst4MvxPCx4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lst4MvxPCx4)<SEP>YouTube Video: k8iO5daXllM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k8iO5daXllM)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vNj7OSHos1I)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Problem";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real content about the entity \"Problem\".

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The descriptions 1 through 8 are the key parts here. The rest is instructions on how to process them. The task is to synthesize these descriptions into a clean summary without any of the meta-text.

Looking at the descriptions:

1. Problem is an external challenge, minor to major, resolved through suffering or positive approach.
2. Similar to 1, mentions responses depend on suffering or beautiful state.
3. Distinguishes external origin from internal suffering.
4. Problem as underlying issue misattributed to external factors (e.g., B score) not self-image.
5. Problem as underlying issue (e.g., self-image fixation) causing suffering, not surface challenge.
6 &7: Unresolved societal/personal issues leading to fear and hurdles.
8: Central theme in various forms like relationships, finance, health.

The instructions mention handling contradictions between 4 and 5. So, need to present both viewpoints. Also, the summary should be in paragraphs, starting with \"Problem is...\", covering all key points without exceeding 600 tokens.

Now, I need to structure this into 1-4 sentences. Let's start with the main definition: Problem as an external challenge, ranging from minor to major, requiring resolution through suffering or positive approach. Then mention that responses depend on the state (suffering or positive). Next, distinguish from internal suffering by external origin. Then, note the two viewpoints from 4 and 5: underlying issue misattributed to external factors vs. underlying issue perpetuating suffering. Also, include unresolved societal/personal issues leading to fear and hurdles, and that it's a central theme in""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-b9eed6b91a21f212612d0bb96c4d8857<SEP>chunk-ddc2a8c2bf46af1d243c4bae41044efd<SEP>chunk-98ebbba09ead01df2486b7e4f58bcc9b<SEP>chunk-6202900249469971e378d57b74b99662<SEP>chunk-87e2f7787298d3205ec139c556ef83c0<SEP>chunk-53efe9fd171ffdc347c0abe139250e7d<SEP>chunk-5ccc31c8e1d16623e7633752bbd5a9ab<SEP>chunk-9f51181a0a82fab99daeacb192359f2b<SEP>chunk-2abf9b76c25a40660c2457bb0ad9b00e<SEP>chunk-539d32cffeac32af158844b70b3aafe4<SEP>chunk-d9460f64cea48e6bb2a99898a9572005<SEP>chunk-c47a850c80a21ed6c67cbed2bc4b8ec0<SEP>chunk-bb8c7007984e1dbf803d7545148dee09";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779723396"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

