  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M7ItOHTrvz8)<SEP>YouTube Video: I6yC-aUQUvw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I6yC-aUQUvw)<SEP>YouTube Video: CrZuPkgwA6Q (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CrZuPkgwA6Q)<SEP>YouTube Video: YkIBYppBtro (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YkIBYppBtro)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RvgN5Mfbd5A)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """The relation 'Questions' is defined as interrogative sentences used to pose inquiries, which are central to the original text's structure. The series of questions within the prompt are identified as Content entities, and they are explored by both ancient civilizations and contemporary times, forming the core of cultural and intellectual exploration. Four existential questions about purpose, effort, and life change are central to this exploration.

Philosophical and self-reflective inquiries about friendship dynamics are also a key aspect of Questions, including the differentiation between toxic and beneficial relationships and personal growth. Additionally, Questions encompass inquiries about relationship dynamics that a spiritual vision helps answer, and during discussions, corrected questions are raised to seek answers related to overcoming crises.

Multiple descriptions highlight that Questions serve as a fundamental mechanism for posing and addressing a wide range of inquiries, from existential concerns to interpersonal dynamics, and they are consistently referenced across various contexts, underscoring their importance in both historical and modern intellectual discourse.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779675653"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Questions" .

