  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "person";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Ravana is a complex character from the Ramayana, portrayed as a scholar-king with internal conflicts and destructive tendencies despite his virtues.<SEP>Ravana is a mythological figure depicted as a man with ten heads, symbolizing his inner conflict and self-destructive tendencies due to dissenting values and obsessive desires.<SEP>Ravana is a figure who succumbed to conflicting desires despite knowing their destructive consequences, leading to his downfall and the collapse of his kingdom.<SEP>Ravana, the ten-headed king, symbolizes internal conflict between desires and moral dilemmas in the context of action.<SEP>Ravana is a historical figure from the Ramayana, depicted as a conflicted king whose inner war between dissenting values led to self-destruction and destruction of his kingdom.<SEP>Ravana is a figure from mythology who struggled with inner conflict and desires, leading to his downfall and the impact on his kingdom.`<SEP>Ravana is a historical figure from the Ramayana, depicted as a conflicted king whose inner turmoil led to self-destruction and downfall." .

