  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text is mostly developer instructions and repetitive prompts, but there's a mention of \"Respectful and forgiving\" being a term that's correctly written.

First, I need to identify the real content. The repeated sentences say that \"Respectful and forgiving is a term that was correctly written.\" The rest is just instructions on how to format the summary, which I need to ignore. Since all the descriptions are identical, combining them just repeats the same point. The key fact here is that the term is correctly written. There's no deeper spiritual teaching beyond that. The entity name is given as \"Respectful and forgiving,\" so the clean description should mention that it's a term correctly written. I need to make sure not to include any of the developer notes or formatting instructions. The output should be a concise, plain English sentence without any extra formatting. Since the only information is that it's a correctly written term, that's all I can extract. No other spiritual concepts are present here. So the final answer should be that single sentence.
</think>

Respectful and forgiving is a term that has been correctly written.""";
