<urn:mukthiguru:Run-on%20Sentence> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-u6ZDfHdB54)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bSyewSnu2Ak)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=207izZBbqVg)<SEP>YouTube Video: I6yC-aUQUvw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I6yC-aUQUvw)<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: OnAAtrwsfOc (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OnAAtrwsfOc)<SEP>YouTube Video: pPHQMD3w9-s (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPHQMD3w9-s)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Run-on Sentence";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-0f5e9ea66f1f177a0f68566957d7e46e<SEP>chunk-9cae7143f497353be3068de2f13fe25c<SEP>chunk-41070a47242b017794bd4b01d9403428<SEP>chunk-ff94932b6f3b0d226dc634858c45e539<SEP>chunk-c7379196e71801ae32380230fbd6d871<SEP>chunk-87c7719422a9d8333cc199f60bc9b163<SEP>chunk-4b35201ea3b2c1a816e4f9f7600e1284<SEP>chunk-f56196cf5558ef3761957d9648db2990<SEP>chunk-98921940959422839d1d78085fa664be";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Run-on Sentence is a grammatical structure characterized by the improper joining of multiple independent clauses without appropriate punctuation or conjunctions. This results in an unbroken, complex sentence that can affect readability. In the source text, such a structure may be employed stylistically to convey a poetic flow, and it is sometimes viewed as a stylistic choice within the text. However, it is also recognized as a structural issue in the original text, which is often addressed during editing to improve clarity. The original mantra or text may present this as a single, long sentence lacking proper punctuation, and it is identified in the transcription as phrases that are improperly concatenated.

While some descriptions emphasize its stylistic use, others highlight the need for correction, reflecting a dual perspective. Overall, the run-on sentence is a grammatical phenomenon that can serve both stylistic and problematic functions, requiring careful consideration during editing.<SEP>A run-on sentence is a grammatical error where multiple independent clauses are incorrectly joined without proper punctuation or conjunctions.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779673177"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

