  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Sacredness is a concept where something becomes sacred when it is perceived as irreplaceable, leading to deep fulfillment and connection.<SEP>Sacredness is a concept discussed in the text with repeated usage.<SEP>Sacredness refers to a profound sense of reverence or spiritual significance, discussed in the context of clunky phrasing examples.<SEP>A concept stated as correct in the input text.<SEP>Sacredness refers to the quality of being worthy of reverence, often experienced in moments of profound connection such as the presence of a newborn or the loss of a loved one.<SEP>Sacredness refers to the quality of being worthy of reverence, often experienced in moments of profound connection such as the presence of a newborn or the loss of a loved one.<SEP>Sacredness refers to the sense of reverence and holiness associated with love, particularly in the context of newborns and loved ones.";
