<urn:mukthiguru:Safety> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-e22181d45ff680a216a2e1e3bb46c19d";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=77dJnbTCwsA)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779719900"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Safety is a concept that describes a leader's focus on protecting the nation and its people. It emphasizes the responsibility of leaders to ensure the security and well-being of the country and its citizens. This focus on protection is central to the role of leadership, as it underpins the stability and prosperity of the nation.

In governance, safety translates into policies and actions aimed at safeguarding the population from threats, whether they are physical, economic, or social. Leaders who prioritize safety work to create an environment where the nation's interests and its people are shielded from harm, fostering trust and cohesion.

The notion of safety extends beyond mere physical security to include economic stability and social welfare. By addressing these dimensions, safety becomes a comprehensive strategy for national development. It ensures that the nation can progress while maintaining the protection of its citizens, making safety an essential principle for effective leadership.<SEP>Safety pertains to a leader's focus on protecting the nation and its people.<SEP>Safety pertains to a leader's focus on protecting the nation and its people.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Safety" .

