  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Sages of India";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content about the \"Sages of India\" from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and repeated mentions.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual teachings or factual content. The key points mentioned are that the Sages of India are ancient scholars who developed Sanskrit for spiritual practices. They are a group of enlightened sages associated with the origins of yoga, original practitioners of yoga, and their disciples sought enlightenment. They are from ancient India and known for deliberate seclusion.

I need to remove all the instructions about formatting, token limits, and the repetitive mentions. The main elements to include are their role in developing Sanskrit, their association with yoga's origins, being enlightened sages, and their disciples' pursuit. Also, they are a group from ancient India.

I should condense this into 1-4 sentences without bullet points or headers. Let me check if there's any other info. The text repeats the same points multiple times, so I just need to present the unique facts once. Make sure to mention their full name at the beginning as per the instructions. Avoid any mention of the developer's requirements. Alright, that should cover it.
</think>

The Sages of India were ancient scholars and enlightened sages from ancient India, credited with developing Sanskrit and its application in spiritual practices. They are recognized as the original practitioners and early proponents of yoga, with its origins deeply tied to their teachings. Known for deliberate seclusion, they attracted disciples seeking enlightenment and were central to the transmission of spiritual knowledge. Their legacy remains foundational to India's spiritual and philosophical traditions.""" .

