  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content about Samskaras from the contaminated text. The contaminated text has a lot of developer instructions and processing steps, but I need to focus only on the real spiritual teachings.

First, I'll look through the contaminated text. The key part is the list of descriptions provided. The descriptions mention that Samskaras are inherited tendencies or impressions from ancestors, which can be positive or negative. They are deeper than memories, influence behavior, and are part of karmic and psychological concepts. Some descriptions mention transmission from father to child, others from ancestors. There's also mention of fear, conflict, and hate being passed down.

I need to combine these points into a concise description. The main elements are: inherited tendencies/impressions, transmission from ancestors or father, positive/negative or fear/conflict/hate, influence on behavior and unconscious processes, and their role in karmic and psychological contexts. I should avoid any mention of the processing steps or instructions. Also, check for duplicates and ensure all key points are covered without exceeding the length. Make sure it's in plain English, 1-4 sentences, and starts with the entity name.
</think>

Samskaras are inherited mental impressions or tendencies transmitted from ancestors or parents, influencing behavior and unconscious processes. These can manifest as wholesome or unwholesome traits, including fear, conflict, and hate, and are linked to karmic and psychological concepts. They operate deeper than ordinary memories, creating repetitive patterns across generations.""";
