<urn:mukthiguru:Sattva> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Sattva is a concept in Hindu philosophy denoting purity, balance, and a state of flow.<SEP>Sattva is a state of flow characterized by the absence of agitation and associated with positive emotions like love, peace, joy, and gratitude.<SEP>Sattva is a state of calmness and contentment, one of the three gunas (qualities) in Hindu philosophy.` -> Correct.<SEP>Sattva represents a spiritual quality symbolizing purity and balance in the scripture.<SEP>Sattva is a concept related to being calm and contented, and is part of a seeker's journey.<SEP>Sattva is a quality of calm and contentment.<SEP>Sattva represents a state of calmness, contentment, and freedom from desire, often associated with spiritual equilibrium.";
