  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Self is understood as the individual's internal relationship with themselves, encompassing both moments of care and dissatisfaction. It also represents an individual's consciousness and identity, described as a playground for intelligence and creativity. In this sense, the self is established in itself, characterized by self-awareness and alignment with one's senses, breath, and inner divine.

During Kundalini awakening, the self is experienced as the true nature of existence, embodying universal oneness and interconnectedness with the universe. The sense of self can expand or be absent in certain states of consciousness, reflecting its fluid nature.

Self-perception and identity are further shaped by societal beauty norms and personal growth, influencing how the self is understood and expressed. These aspects collectively define the self as a multifaceted construct that integrates personal awareness, creative potential, and relational dynamics.<SEP>Self is defined by ideals and is central to moral judgment.<SEP>Self is the individual's own consciousness and sense of being, which expands and transforms.<SEP>Self is the individual's own consciousness and sense of being, which expands and transforms.<SEP>The concept of \"self\" relates to the individual's sense of identity and awareness expanding to include others.<SEP>The concept of \"self\" relates to the individual's sense of identity and awareness expanding to include others.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Self" .

