  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "The practice of self-criticism observed with kindness rather than anger, framed as a natural human tendency.<SEP>Self-criticism involves internalized judgment that diminishes self-worth and perpetuates emotional suffering.`<SEP>Self-criticism is the act of judging oneself harshly, often manifesting as anger or jealousy toward aspects of one's identity.<SEP>The act of judging oneself harshly, resulting in dissatisfaction and self-doubt.<SEP>Self-criticism involves constant commentary on oneself, driving comparison and inner war.<SEP>Self-criticism refers to the habit of judging oneself harshly, leading to emotional distress." .

