  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Self-preoccupation describes a state of being overly focused on one's own thoughts and feelings, creating cycles of internal conflict.<SEP>A habitual state of being overly focused on one's own emotions and needs, leading to strained relationships.` The description is a bit long. The instructions say \"concise yet comprehensive\". This might be okay, but I'll keep it in mind.<SEP>A habitual state of being overly focused on one's own emotions and needs, leading to strained relationships.` This is a valid entity.<SEP>Self-preoccupation is a concept that is emphasized as a negative trait in relationships.<SEP>Being caught up in one's own thinking and thought-created miseries leads to alienation.<SEP>Excessive focus on one's own thoughts and emotions, leading to disconnection from others.";
