<urn:mukthiguru:Serene%20Mind%20Practice> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hwNlLB1sze0)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M7ItOHTrvz8)<SEP>YouTube Video: zGOKGrTNlk4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zGOKGrTNlk4)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Serene Mind Practice";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779396467"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Serene Mind Practice is a meditation technique designed to dissolve anxiety, desperation, and self‑obsession by cultivating present‑moment awareness and a sense of connection. It involves observing emotions without becoming attached to them, thereby reducing suffering and fostering serenity.  

The practice is structured as a three‑step meditation, though some sources describe it as a three‑minute technique, emphasizing its brevity and accessibility. It is presented as a simple yet effective method to break anxiety habits, release fear, and shift consciousness. Brain‑training aspects are noted, with the technique claimed to activate specific brain regions, thereby altering consciousness and external outcomes.  

Serene Mind Practice is used globally by a diverse range of individuals, including leaders, spiritual seekers, teenagers, and children, to prevent obsessive states, enhance clarity, and manage stress in various situations. It is also described as a mental technique to move from self‑obsession to a state of serenity and as a pathway to accessing universal intelligence, offering a method to release anxiety and fear while cultivating a more balanced mental state.<SEP>Serene mind practice is a technique recommended to dissolve suffering and find solutions to problems.<SEP>Serene mind practice is a technique to dissolve suffering and problems through mental connection.<SEP>Serene mind practice is a method to dissolve suffering and anxiety, facilitating transition to stillness.<SEP>Serene mind practice is a method to prevent the buildup of suffering by consciously acknowledging and addressing disturbances.<SEP>Serene mind practice involves intentional awareness to manage inner disturbances and prevent suffering buildup.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "method";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-b4387a01e271d1d16068a0288faa84e5<SEP>chunk-46f092e49beb29848499bc5cec4e1faf<SEP>chunk-0b9ac55d2cab188fc69b15917905c7be<SEP>chunk-214089f71bed8468f80247a24979283e<SEP>chunk-999192b96103e7c498639cfadd062722<SEP>chunk-5b0bc29474343c900abfcb530ac6bf39<SEP>chunk-a8aa437c4036f2bcb15546966bd2e573<SEP>chunk-bbc81bf6a0558d20de7cf1bfde2d1f2a<SEP>chunk-956d12a94e0e0bb6b9859844aca052b9<SEP>chunk-0de990c9c98448c49e9565dc513c171a<SEP>chunk-e7c9f032dc546ceb8596a807018125ca<SEP>chunk-0ddbd4446b0368311d8844f5869734c4<SEP>chunk-28084224d33efa95fcb7e18cd0d14748" .

