  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Smallpox is a deadly disease that historically caused high mortality and cultural shifts in naming practices and social norms.<SEP>Smallpox is a deadly disease that caused widespread mortality and blindness, used as a historical comparison to COVID-19.<SEP>...\" which is incomplete. That's a formatting error. Also, the original input mentions \"racially segregated quarantine\" leading to apartheid in South Africa. The previous output had a relation between Plague and Europe regarding hygiene, but maybe missed the connection to South Africa's segregation.<SEP>...\" which is incomplete. The correct line should have all five fields.";
