  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Soul Sync Meditation";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-02f292000f544446b15f0519998d1dbc<SEP>chunk-6aebd99b80a116244470eacf183c4202<SEP>chunk-61c0437442c1a79367c1612c9b022b8f<SEP>chunk-bcc3c744d91ef9d256a5b7e4cc0ab412";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "method";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes developer instructions and multiple descriptions of \"Soul Sync Meditation.\" My job is to sift through all that and pull out the real spiritual content.

First, I need to identify the key points from the descriptions. The first description mentions it's a structured practice for inner calm and dissolving ego, but it's noted as a duplicate and incorrect. The second says it's for dissolving stress and fostering calm. The fourth and fifth/sixth mention chanting and vibration or mantras to expand consciousness. The seventh and eighth talk about breathwork and visualization to align with Universal Consciousness.

The developer notes mention conflicts, but I need to focus on the actual content. The main elements seem to be: structured practice, chanting/vibration/mantras, breathwork/visualization, aligning with Universal Consciousness, dissolving ego and stress, fostering calm, expanding consciousness. 

I should combine these into a coherent description without the developer's notes. Make sure to mention the methods (chanting, breathwork, visualization), the purpose (inner calm, dissolving ego, stress, expanding consciousness), and the alignment with Universal Consciousness. Avoid any mention of duplicates or instructions. Keep it concise, 1-4 sentences. Let me check if all the key points are covered. Yes, that should do it.
</think>

Soul Sync Meditation is a structured practice involving breathwork, visualization, and chanting (such as mantras or vibration) to align with Universal Consciousness. It aims to dissolve ego-driven patterns, reduce stress and suffering, and foster inner calm by expanding consciousness beyond limited mental associations. The practice facilitates personal transformation through sustained focus on universal awareness.""" .

