<urn:mukthiguru:Species%20Survival> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779656827"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Species Survival is the process by which a biological species persists over time. It is maintained through mechanisms such as extended reproductive roles in certain members, which contribute to the species' continuity. Species Survival also involves the continuation of the species via reproduction and the transfer of cultural knowledge across generations. Moreover, it is underpinned by a biological imperative that encourages evolutionary traits, such as extended lifespan, to secure the continuity of life.

The concept of Species Survival encompasses both biological and cultural dimensions. Biologically, it ensures that species reproduce and pass on genetic material, while culturally, knowledge and practices are transmitted, enhancing adaptability. This dual mechanism allows species to respond to environmental changes and maintain resilience. The biological imperative that drives traits like extended lifespan further supports the long-term persistence of species, ensuring that life continues across generations.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: QzJ_Ft1de1o (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QzJ_Ft1de1o)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Species Survival";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-efef91f79f63a3dccc0da4a26bee1fef<SEP>chunk-bc3611b977330c3669fa3dd3bfb5860e<SEP>chunk-f8d4df49e2bb59337f3b12dcef1d6f2c";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

