<urn:mukthiguru:Spirituality> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Spirituality is a philosophical and religious dimension of human experience that also serves as a domain where future leaders apply awakened consciousness to foster inner growth. It is referenced as a realm of existential and moral understanding within the context of leadership, where leaders are instructed to lead. This concept integrates philosophical, religious, and mystical aspects, and is regarded as a framework for inner growth and moral understanding, especially in leadership contexts.

Spirituality is described as a mystic science of consciousness and its awakening, which can lead to enlightenment and either liberation from suffering or transformation of personal experience. Some accounts emphasize the transformation of personal experience, while others focus on liberation from suffering. Overall, spirituality is presented as a journey toward enlightenment, with the dual outcomes of personal transformation and liberation.

The concept is centered on spiritual awakening and connection to higher consciousness. It is an inward journey focused on inner awakening and living in an awakened state, distinct from religious teachings. Additionally, spirituality is a discipline grappling with death through enlightenment. It is also a force that can soothe emotional wounds or ignite revolutionary change, requiring collective action from various societal groups.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Spirituality";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
