<urn:mukthiguru:Stressful%20State> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779560342"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Stressful State is a mental and emotional condition marked by tension, anxiety, negative emotions, lack of joy, self-preoccupation, and habitual focus on past or future events. It is characterized by self-centric thinking, reactive patterns, and a sense of being overwhelmed, leading to poor outcomes in daily life. The state is one of two possible existence states, binary with a beautiful state, and is considered the default human state when not actively choosing the beautiful state. It is the opposite of calm, joyful, and beautiful states, and is associated with disconnection and suffering.

The manifestations of a stressful state include tension, anger, fear, frustration, and possibly loneliness. Triggers can be past or present circumstances, emotional turmoil, or any situation that induces anxiety. Associated behaviors involve overcomplication, irrationality, agitation, and emotional separation. Cognitively, the state features internal conflict, confusion, repetitive thinking, and poor decision-making. Consequences of being in a stressful state include health risks, unwise choices, and poor outcomes, as well as a general inability to experience life fully.

A concise description of the stressful state is that it is a mental state characterized by tension and anxiety, leading to inferior responses to challenges. This definition aligns with the broader description, emphasizing the negative impact on decision-making and overall functioning. The stressful state, when not consciously chosen, defaults to the human condition, making it a prevalent and often unconscious state for many individuals.<SEP>Stressful State signifies a mindset marked by anxiety, conflict, and lack of confidence, driving negative outcomes.`<SEP>Stressful State signifies a mindset marked by anxiety, conflict, and lack of confidence, driving negative outcomes.`<SEP>A state of consciousness marked by anxiety, pressure, and negative emotional responses.<SEP>A state marked by tension and negativity that hinders personal and collective growth.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
