<urn:mukthiguru:Student> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q4QyNologtw)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y4ZR5U8VuQY)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DLb6hDIhmg)<SEP>YouTube Video: mmpmX3-qfc4 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mmpmX3-qfc4)<SEP>YouTube Video: _GEMrEWCiXw (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_GEMrEWCiXw)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-aab1cb8ec22effc5abff8b57b4b03ad3<SEP>chunk-f02bf32393ef9705110f96bbc12d8064<SEP>chunk-0e75139b40ca183a0159101fa414702c<SEP>chunk-b1768835e61a5423d2655e03e093fded<SEP>chunk-2ed6c538824d03e53845129e9fe68f60<SEP>chunk-8fe41869f1b0fa2b6e988f652c7091c5<SEP>chunk-e27a47feac82bbd6f6606fd0582e97d1";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Student";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779652844"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text is a mix of developer instructions and some real content about the entity \"Student\". My job is to sift through all that and pull out only the spiritual or factual content related to the Student.

First, I need to identify the real content. The contaminated text includes a lot of instructions about how to process the input, like handling JSON objects, output formats, conflict resolution, etc. But the actual spiritual content is in the bullet points under \"We need to integrate these.\" Let me look at those.

The bullet points mention a student discovering Swadharma in culinary arts through meditation and overcoming societal pressures. Another student attended youth courses, dealt with depression and family pressure, found clarity. There's also Krishnaji and an incident with a migrant worker. Another student is a follower of a teacher questioning Brahman after being hurt by an elephant. Then there are generic points about students manifesting excellence and feeling inadequate in academics.

I need to synthesize these into a coherent summary. The key here is to group the specific narratives and the generic definitions. The spiritual elements here are Swadharma (a concept from Hinduism about one's duty or purpose), meditation, divine guidance, overcoming societal pressures, and the philosophical questioning of Brahman (the ultimate reality in Hinduism). The other points about depression, family pressure, and academic comparison might be more psychological but still relevant to the spiritual journey.

I should start by stating the entity name \"Student\" as per the instructions. Then mention the generic aspects: individuals in educational activities, manifestations of excellence, and academic comparison issues. Then move to the specific spiritual narratives: Swadharma in culinary arts through meditation, overcoming societal pressures, the Krishnaji incident, the teacher's questioning of Brahman. Also, the student who struggled with depression and found clarity through a program.

I need to make sure""" .

