  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Stylistic Weakness is a term used to denote issues or deficiencies in the style of an original text. These weaknesses can manifest as problems with clarity, coherence, tone, or other stylistic elements that affect the overall quality of the writing. Identifying and addressing stylistic weaknesses is important for improving the readability and effectiveness of the text.

Addressing stylistic weaknesses involves analyzing the text for specific style-related problems and implementing revisions to enhance clarity, consistency, and overall impact.<SEP>Stylistic weaknesses refer to issues in the original text's style.<SEP>Stylistic weaknesses refer to issues in the original text's style.<SEP>Stylistic weaknesses refer to issues in the original text's style.<SEP>Stylistic weaknesses refer to issues in the original text's style.<SEP>Stylistic weaknesses refer to issues in the original text's style.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Stylistic Weakness" .

