<urn:mukthiguru:Subject-Verb%20Agreement> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Grammatical rule governing verb conjugation for compound subjects, central to the analysis of the phrase \"Discrimination and separation.\"<SEP>Subject-verb agreement refers to grammatical rules governing verb forms based on subject number and person.<SEP>A grammatical rule requiring plural verbs for compound subjects, which was violated in the original sentence.<SEP>A grammatical rule requiring plural verbs for compound subjects, which was violated in the original sentence.<SEP>Subject-verb agreement refers to grammatical rules governing verb forms based on subject number and person.";
