  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Suering states such as frustration, disappointment, jealousy, or hate are described as destructive, leading to chaos and mounting problems in personal and societal life.<SEP>Suering states (likely a typo for \"suffering states\") describe emotional conditions where individuals dwell on past pain or stress.<SEP>Emotional or mental states characterized by suffering, such as anxiety or loneliness.<SEP>Emotional or psychological conditions characterized by lingering pain or distress, referenced in the text as \"suering.\"<SEP>Suering states include boredom, irritation, discontent, anger, fear, and existential despair, intensifying into severe conditions.<SEP>Suering states are unconscious, deeply ingrained emotional patterns that prevent individuals from experiencing wholeness, calm, joy, and courage. They often originate epigenetically, prenatally, during early childhood, or later in life.<SEP>Suering states encompass negative emotional and existential conditions like fear, anger, and sadness, described as daymares that obscure true consciousness." .

<urn:mukthiguru:Suering%20States%20of%20Consciousness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf";
