  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Swadharma refers to a career path aligned with one's core nature, causing well-being to oneself and others, and driven by passion and love.<SEP>The principle of following one's true calling with love and passion, central to the program's teachings.<SEP>Swadharma refers to the concept of living in alignment with one's true purpose, which is highlighted as essential for creating societal revolutions.<SEP>Swadharma refers to one's inherent purpose or duty that becomes apparent through self-transcendence.<SEP>Swadharma refers to one's inherent purpose or duty that becomes apparent through self-transcendence.<SEP>Swadharma refers to a career path or purpose born from a state of connection and awareness of global crises.<SEP>Swadharma refers to one's unique purpose or duty derived from an expanded state of connection, emphasizing alignment with existence itself." .

