<urn:mukthiguru:Terrell%20Monash%20University> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Terrell Monash University";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept from the contaminated text. The contaminated text is a mix of developer instructions and some content about Terrell Monash University.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual content. The main points from the descriptions are that the university collaborates with Over Know Academy to offer a program combining academic and spiritual education. They mention both a collaborative partnership and an association. The key elements are the integration of academic and spiritual education, the partnership, and the association.

The developer instructions include things like structuring paragraphs, avoiding redundancy, and token limits. I need to remove all that. The actual content is in the bullet points under the first description and the repeated ones. The repeated ones just state the association, but the first one adds the collaboration and the integrated program.

So, the clean description should mention the university as an educational institution associated with Over Know Academy, their collaborative partnership, the program that combines academic and spiritual education, and that the relationship includes both association and collaboration. Also, note that multiple descriptions confirm this.

I need to present this in 1-4 sentences, plain English, no bullet points or headers. Let me check if there's any spiritual teaching here. The integration of academic and spiritual education is the main spiritual concept. The rest is about the relationship structure. So the clean output should focus on that integration and the partnership/association.
</think>

Terrell Monash University is an educational institution associated with the Over Know Academy program. It collaborates with Over Know Academy to offer a program that integrates academic and spiritual education, combining academic learning with spiritual development. The relationship between the university and the program is characterized by both a collaborative partnership and an association, with multiple descriptions confirming this dual connection.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Qu5IQo0ghbs (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qu5IQo0ghbs)";
