<urn:mukthiguru:The%20Academy> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes both developer instructions and the real content about The Academy.

First, I need to identify the real spiritual teachings or concepts. The descriptions mention things like a sense of family, transformative practices, consciousness transformation through philosophy and meditation, hands-on operation, courses, teaching, charities, global businesses, and specific events involving Krishnaji, Diego, and two children.

The developer parts are the instructions about synthesizing a list, handling conflicts, and formatting requirements. I need to remove all of that. The key is to focus on the descriptions under the \"Description List\" and the integrated key info at the end.

Looking at the descriptions, there are duplicates (4 and 5 are the same), so I should mention that once. The events involving Krishnaji and Diego, and the two children's experience, are separate aspects but part of The Academy's activities. I need to combine all the unique points without the developer notes.

So, the clean description should include The Academy as an educational institution with a family-like environment, transformative practices, consciousness transformation through philosophy and meditation, hands-on courses, charities, global businesses, and the specific events. I need to present this in 1-4 sentences, plain English, no bullet points or headers. Let me structure that.
</think>

The Academy is an educational institution fostering a sense of family and shared connection among students. It offers transformative practices, including philosophy and meditation, to help individuals overcome challenges and create new destinies through consciousness transformation. The Academy operates hands-on, designing courses and teaching higher classes while supporting global businesses and charities that impact villagers and students. It also served as the location for Krishnaji’s special process with Diego and hosted a transformative spiritual experience for two children.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-c219578ff4da1678ae1ff2890bf677ec<SEP>chunk-be5e79cc66746a0a24382426cfe2a8ff<SEP>chunk-7769be7ae0544b9b85386becf7e58bed<SEP>chunk-64534fa37e2772d16d26e6098d4409b0<SEP>chunk-1ba7f5be1d21e67ddd5d6d9988215271<SEP>chunk-999192b96103e7c498639cfadd062722<SEP>chunk-ac2f8cb722c994eb19c13fbd7a35cc4f";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "organization";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "The Academy";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779443249"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long> .

