<urn:mukthiguru:Thoughts> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779672418"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-0b93a19f07fdaada8a87bb7bfa37fae9<SEP>chunk-bd988ca2fbb6c189e4b536ea7d78104c<SEP>chunk-a395387e60480713a88c70d27d01c1ab<SEP>chunk-23221c5b17e3851e48fb2c99d16575d0<SEP>chunk-f75c5d6ff6cf90a0c79623ead0773fbc<SEP>chunk-ba586743a140b7df40d5cacb7f238ed9<SEP>chunk-e7076c6d9101be02063cc3fee9b2fbba<SEP>chunk-e56919e461f379123fc8b4b2380a2a52<SEP>chunk-b04f7ebc196bc2024dc00fdd71633076<SEP>chunk-295ece324351da0c7194c4e2d4f58e99<SEP>chunk-53e525d93caa11247db9588a7b9a8e7a<SEP>chunk-331ce489e777434104c9abde748a4203<SEP>chunk-a806b7026395d82c6e1fe100191449c6<SEP>chunk-9174f4aac6278b492855cabdc7a615b1";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Thoughts";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KTe11DlB4QI)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jW3JDLY0cDA)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OWMBvMlGWTA)<SEP>YouTube Video: 6j6EGVpQkI8 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6j6EGVpQkI8)<SEP>YouTube Video: ajMAwlKh3YM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajMAwlKh3YM)<SEP>YouTube Video: ffhDTzE4nDU (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ffhDTzE4nDU)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc8f9ZasRRM)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Thoughts are mental processes that can repeat over time and contribute to the formation of one's internal state. They are described as processes that can be repeated, and in some contexts, they may be considered neutral, but generally they are part of the mind's ongoing activity.

In many cases, thoughts exhibit a negativity bias, with a majority—83%—described as negative and repetitive. Other sources report that thoughts are categorized as repetitive (80-85%) and negative (70%), with an average of 15,000-60,000 per day. This bias includes self-obsessed tendencies.

Mental processes are observed during meditation, not attributed to a self. Additionally, mental states, including thoughts, can be influenced by the emotional energy of food and environments.

The average number of thoughts per day is estimated at 15,000–60,000, reflecting the high volume and repetitive nature of mental activity.

These descriptions collectively highlight that thoughts are dynamic, often negative, and subject to external influences such as diet and surroundings, while also being observable in meditative states without self-referential attribution.<SEP>The mind is composed of thoughts, with an average of 15,000 to 60,000 per day.""" .

