  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real spiritual teachings about \"Transformation.\" My job is to sift through all that and pull out only the relevant spiritual concepts.

First, I need to identify the key elements mentioned in the input. The long description talks about inner change, consciousness, spiritual vision, shifting from self-obsessed to unified states, parent-child relationships, healing, growth, culture of support, destiny, and more. The short descriptions mention conscious evolution and societal structures, and there's a specific instance of a nine-day personal change.

The developer instructions are about synthesizing summaries, handling conflicts, integrating key information, and formatting the output. I need to ignore all of that. The actual content is the spiritual aspects of Transformation. 

I should start by defining Transformation as a process involving inner change and consciousness. Then mention the shift from I-consciousness to One-consciousness. Include elements like healing, growth, and societal shifts. Also, note the nine-day example as a specific instance. Make sure it's in plain English, 1-4 sentences, no bullet points or headers. Check that all the key points from the contaminated text are covered without any extra fluff. Avoid mentioning the developer stuff. Let me piece that together concisely.
</think>

Transformation is a process of profound inner change driven by spiritual vision and conscious evolution, marked by a shift from self-centered awareness (I-consciousness) to unified consciousness (One-consciousness). It encompasses healing, growth, and relational dynamics, often manifesting through holistic shifts in personal and societal structures, supported by a culture of empathy and shared destiny. This process enables individuals to realize their potential, align with deeper existential experiences, and move toward collective unity. It may also manifest as an intense personal transformation over specific periods, such as the nine-day example described, reflecting""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Transformation" .

