<urn:mukthiguru:Unhappiness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Unhappiness";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Unhappiness is an emotional state that arises from self‑preoccupation and unresolved inner conflict. It can also be triggered by societal norms and a lack of authenticity, and by self‑criticism or other internal tensions. In some perspectives, unhappiness is linked to stagnant or superficial relationships, serving as a breeding ground for inner turmoil and dissatisfaction. The state is described as a condition of distress or sorrow that may be shared with others, and it can manifest as a breeding ground for inner conflict and dissatisfaction.

The experience of unhappiness is often characterized by inner turmoil, dissatisfaction, and a sense of distress or sorrow. It may result from unresolved inner conflict, self‑preoccupation, or external factors such as societal expectations and lack of authenticity. In some accounts, it is portrayed as a consequence of societal norms and lack of authenticity, not resolved by external solutions.

Addressing unhappiness can involve supportive responses from others, such as Krishnaji’s empathetic engagement with the narrator’s sadness. It also includes conscious efforts to alleviate inner disturbances, connection via empathy, and the cultivation of deeper, more meaningful relationships. Some descriptions emphasize that unhappiness can be shared, allowing for mutual support and understanding.

While some viewpoints suggest that unhappiness stems from self‑preoccupation and inner conflict, others highlight the role of societal norms, lack of authenticity, and stagnant relationships. The entity is thus a multifaceted emotional state that may require both internal reflection and external support to be mitigated. It is noted that unhappiness can be a shared experience, and that addressing it may involve empathy, conscious effort, and supportive interactions.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779347541"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: PFNP4c1cOSI (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PFNP4c1cOSI)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-c756fff1f643175625bc8f48eb702151<SEP>chunk-53499f381af4c99f9a37a7d03455b285<SEP>chunk-9398fca4f7667d8c5a5db620f32a2795<SEP>chunk-c85036006eb9517f84fbb3ee7717030e<SEP>chunk-5c02e046d7832f0655166e3f716f3e10<SEP>chunk-66f6c16a0cd4b4ef4b399e98335000b4<SEP>chunk-5506ec1bf2947c78c3b169a20af36482<SEP>chunk-959b75d8730e8069b5cdeee7b801f17f<SEP>chunk-ac599df176221b3c1e3e9b33cb62fa37" .

