  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Unity is a concept described in the provided descriptions as the recognition of the value in diverse perceptions and the realization of collective peace. Alternatively, it is also described as the realization of the value in diverse perceptions and the foundation for collective peace.

These two perspectives highlight different aspects of the same idea: one emphasizes the act of recognizing the value in varied viewpoints, while the other focuses on the actualization of that value. Both descriptions agree that Unity involves the acknowledgment of value across different perceptions and the establishment of a basis for collective peace. The distinction lies in whether the emphasis is on the cognitive recognition or the practical realization of that value.<SEP>Unity is described as the realization of the value in diverse perceptions and the foundation for collective peace.<SEP>Unity is described as the recognition of the value in diverse perceptions and the realization of collective peace.<SEP>Unity is described as the realization of the value in diverse perceptions and the foundation for collective peace.<SEP>Unity is described as the recognition of the value in diverse perceptions and the realization of collective peace.<SEP>Unity is described as the recognition of the value in diverse perceptions and the realization of collective peace.<SEP>Unity reflects the text’s theme of interconnectedness with the Earth and collective existence.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779659866"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
