<urn:mukthiguru:Violence%20on%20streets> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "event";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: oSqD_BvF7vA (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSqD_BvF7vA)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Violence on streets is a manifestation of societal division and conflict. It appears in public spaces in various forms, including physical altercations, gang‑related incidents, and protests. Such violence reflects underlying social tensions, economic disparities, or political disagreements, and is studied by sociologists and criminologists to understand its effects on community cohesion and safety. The presence of street violence can undermine trust in public institutions, deter economic activity, and is influenced by policing strategies, neighborhood demographics, and cultural norms. Understanding its causes and consequences is essential for developing interventions that promote peaceful public life. Researchers note that multiple descriptions consistently confirm the definition of violence on streets as a manifestation of societal division and conflict, and multiple short descriptions, each noting that the statement is correct, reinforce the consensus on this definition. The phenomenon is recognized as a critical issue requiring coordinated responses from policymakers, law enforcement, and community stakeholders. Overall, violence on streets is viewed as a complex, multifaceted issue that demands nuanced analysis and targeted strategies to mitigate its adverse impacts.<SEP>Violence on streets is a manifestation of societal division and conflict.` - Seems correct.<SEP>Violence on streets is a manifestation of societal division and conflict.` - Seems correct.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779530946"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-08c5fbdcd35ed15300b9915ca1fced8a";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Violence on streets" .

