<urn:mukthiguru:Warring%20Self> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-670e795b68d71dbf734feac6e97cfa1f<SEP>chunk-f184ea56bcea598aa525718d96f6e142<SEP>chunk-afc14563513f7a4dcf36c1ff3fddd517<SEP>chunk-6af7eefe80697b9b2cf1b0520fd6a984";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Warring Self";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "The \"Warring Self\" refers to internal conflicts that manifest as destructive forces when individuals embrace expressions of self-sabotage or negative self-perception.<SEP>Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and self-criticism, as described in the Soul Sync Exercise.<SEP>The Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and discord with oneself and the world.<SEP>Warring Self represents a state of internal conflict and self-criticism, characterized by struggle with oneself and external factors.";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779179356"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Warring-Self%20States> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Warring-Self States";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-6ff356fa9f4583782a04af42a23a7935<SEP>chunk-7146bcb62c68c22b68c6b0cc9e8d3a09<SEP>chunk-6d0566c8fa6f2aed45fb2e69b00761b1<SEP>chunk-246826c01e25761bf87cb37c0f82bbb8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779184130"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "Warring-self states refer to internal conflicts where inner critics divide individuals from their joy and calm.<SEP>Warring-self states are internal conflicts and self-criticism that divide a person's consciousness, leading to comparison and inner war.<SEP>Warring-self states refer to inner critics that tear individuals apart and steal joy and calm from their lives.<SEP>Warring-self states are manifestations of inner critics that divide experiences." .

<urn:mukthiguru:Wars> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Wars";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-e1d5e0073f33e1ee1857e1f6302d5b7f<SEP>chunk-60af06a20529afe356c9b2c29e286a87<SEP>chunk-6fa29767ceb8e0fa67cf872f6c5dc513<SEP>chunk-70484d1909cf7a831cc47f5cf33a0709<SEP>chunk-13f1c611f4cbca7ca30788a6d47f7e15<SEP>chunk-2fcfdd09e7882fdd48ac5703861252ac<SEP>chunk-e13b3b3dd6b43643b1596294c861a1aa<SEP>chunk-3aae932faaf9adc0f11927ad30f84d81";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "YouTube Video: 4LIZkNHlNaM (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4LIZkNHlNaM)<SEP>YouTube Video: aqSM9LwqWgA (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aqSM9LwqWgA)<SEP>YouTube Video: EhY6npcnSs8 (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EhY6npcnSs8)<SEP>YouTube Video: Unknown (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cxgHFX04RtQ)";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779717628"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real content about Wars.

First, I need to identify the key points related to the spiritual or conceptual aspects of Wars. The text mentions that wars are large-scale armed conflicts between nations or groups, linked to global instability. There's a mention of prolonged destruction and destabilization. Then there's a part about some analyses suggesting wars originate from a 'mental infection of violence' within human psychology, which points to internal psychological factors. Consequences include historical examples like the Mahabharata, WWI, and WWII. Triggers are hate speech and social unrest, and some descriptions mention exacerbation by hate speech and division. Also, wars are treated as concepts in video content and are both psychological phenomena and tangible events with far-reaching effects.

I need to synthesize all these points into a concise, clean description without any developer instructions. The output should start with \"Wars are defined as...\" and include all key aspects: definition, causes (hate speech, social unrest, psychological factors), consequences (historical examples), and their dual nature as psychological and tangible events. I should avoid bullet points and headers, keep it in plain English, and ensure it's under 600 tokens. Also, check that all variations are integrated, like combining triggers and exacerbating factors. Make sure not to include any meta-text or instructions from the original prompt.
</think>

Wars are defined as large-scale armed conflicts between nations or groups, often linked to global instability and prolonged destruction. These conflicts can originate from psychological factors such as a \"mental infection of violence\" within human psychology, and are frequently triggered by hate speech, social unrest, or exacerbated by division. Historical examples include the Mahabharata, World War One, and World War Two, which demonstrate their destabilizing, far""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "" .

