<urn:mukthiguru:Wholeness> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Wholeness";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779651357"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Wholeness is a concept that describes a state of completeness, balance, and integration in life. It is a condition of being whole, where emotional completeness and balance are present, yet this state can be obstructed by suffering states. Wholeness is also characterized as a state of being disconnected from self‑preoccupation and aligned with one’s true self. This state is not merely an external condition but a condition to be achieved within oneself, reflecting an inner process of integration and alignment.

Beyond emotional and psychological dimensions, Wholeness is often associated with spiritual fulfillment. It is described as a state of being complete and integrated, which is frequently linked to spiritual experiences and the alignment of one’s soul with a partner, referred to as a soul mate. The unity in consciousness required for spiritual fulfillment and soul‑mate alignment is a core aspect of Wholeness. In essence, Wholeness encompasses a holistic sense of completeness and unity that integrates the self, fosters spiritual growth, and enables alignment with one’s true self""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-c07886881fdb93e8dac5d36189340a55<SEP>chunk-c5db2181b0244c95f353d5c0b1c153ef<SEP>chunk-d97614999399e6f5f1181bdaebd85f12<SEP>chunk-2bd00175db71e25481fb9ce67f057b84<SEP>chunk-c29e446278bb16bd97c026c06682add6<SEP>chunk-7796e9953e60bd3bb11c46251f992983<SEP>chunk-1eb764bde7f7f1e1e97d8931c7b9875e";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source<SEP>YouTube Video: 1nhXsnx5--Y (URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1nhXsnx5--Y)" .

