  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779518424"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual content from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and prompt templates mixed with the real content about World Consciousness.

First, I need to identify the parts that are just instructions or meta-text. The beginning and end have sections like \"We need to synthesize...\" and \"Output the clean description only,\" which are clearly instructions. Then there's a long description that starts with \"We need to integrate all key information...\" which seems to outline the content but is part of the contamination. The short descriptions are mentioned as repeating the same phrase, which is \"World consciousness represents the collective awakening of humanity to unity and wisdom.\"

The real spiritual content is in the long description that talks about World Consciousness as a concept involving interconnectedness, shared purpose, global unity, transformative processes, harmonious ways, common heritage, and its exploration in philosophical, spiritual, and sociological contexts. The short descriptions just repeat the collective awakening part, which is part of the actual content.

I need to combine these elements into a clean 1-4 sentence description. Start with defining World Consciousness, mention the collective awakening, interconnectedness, shared purpose, global unity, transformative process, moving beyond narrow identities, common heritage, and its relevance in addressing global challenges and promoting well-being. Avoid any mention of the instructions or structure like paragraphs. Make sure it's in plain English without bullet points or headers. Check that it's under 4 sentences and only includes the spiritual aspects, not the developer notes.
</think>

World Consciousness is a concept representing the collective awakening of humanity to unity and wisdom, characterized by an awareness of interconnectedness among individuals and societies. It emphasizes shared purpose, global unity, and deeper understanding, fostering a transformative process toward harmonious and cooperative ways of living beyond narrow identities. This state of consciousness is explored in philosophical, spiritual""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "World Consciousness" .

<urn:mukthiguru:World%20Environment%20Day> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and some JSON descriptions about World Environment Day.

First, I need to identify the real content. The descriptions mention that World Environment Day is an annual global event focused on environmental awareness, action, protection, and sustainability. The developer instructions talk about synthesizing the JSON data into a summary, but that's not part of the actual content. The key points from the descriptions are that it's annual, global, focuses on environmental aspects, and includes awareness and action. The UN isn't mentioned in the provided descriptions, so I shouldn't include that even if I know it's true. The task is to only use the given data. The conflicting terms like \"awareness and action\" vs. \"protection and sustainability\" can be combined. The result should be a clean, concise summary without any extra info or formatting. Let me make sure I remove all the instructions and just present the core facts.
</think>

World Environment Day is an annual global event focused on environmental awareness, action, protection, and sustainability. It serves as a platform for international cooperation and raises consciousness about ecological preservation. The observance emphasizes collective responsibility toward sustaining planetary health through conscious practices and policy advocacy.""";
