<urn:mukthiguru:Wounded%20Child> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-e88f2f26245ad8ca0468808d9150fa60<SEP>chunk-41b3a29187ba0c1a38ac4f058b4fd20f<SEP>chunk-4c210ebd42ece17aa2cbb5a935a96e78<SEP>chunk-c0e08ca8392db0f9984988041685087e<SEP>chunk-abf598569eb5f03bc21c09bf7af4abf7<SEP>chunk-8b9c1604faa1ea45879aac48740ef02f<SEP>chunk-42e3465bd48ea87621d94e9d33063209<SEP>chunk-697da9f4d9cac1cfedd243857a8b8ccc<SEP>chunk-b75e52bdeada1ddd1aebcff0a658afb0<SEP>chunk-6e5caa7e31ebe95d72aef04edb890b5c<SEP>chunk-da0dcd44b642ae88bb5ae6bfa953a323<SEP>chunk-5d0f74c4239eabf7a6fea87da28be5d8";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """The Wounded Child is a psychological state rooted in unresolved past trauma, characterized by emotional rigidity and feelings of being unloved or unappreciated, which can hinder personal progress and lead to self-centric misery or half-hearted engagement with life. It contrasts with the Happy Child's state of being, and represents a condition where past disappointment and unmet emotional needs persist into adulthood, influencing behavior and relationships. The Wounded Child can also be viewed as a frozen condition in past pain, shame, and self-judgment, which ties individuals to stagnation.

Additionally, the concept is described as a metaphorical state of carrying past burdens, requiring healing to achieve freedom and joy. This state reflects a deep-seated emotional pain that stems from childhood experiences and continues to affect the individual's present life.

In specific contexts, the Wounded Child is applied to individual identities: for example, it describes Jaya's core identity, where unresolved childhood pain persists despite her outward persona, and it is discussed in Krishnaji's work as inner trauma and past experiences hindering personal growth. These references illustrate how the Wounded Child can be both a general psychological construct and a personal or philosophical framework.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779183769"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Wounded Child" .

<urn:mukthiguru:Wounded%20Child%20State> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-b6d2ea9a34bd43a3b859724cf57d8bec<SEP>chunk-749e889c128e710cc18adc38c4d377cb<SEP>chunk-faa97c15f888df1c3373e6c7826983c8<SEP>chunk-f34d4c3475c783164c62af4dbf5b6c3c<SEP>chunk-c9bf814a48dc1240281eb32fd8bfe8b4<SEP>chunk-da4a30723d6bfb88a08e73a51a9a3d62<SEP>chunk-25634a7e16db511e9e5b4a8597da99fd<SEP>chunk-6b077b95a5e468c5e42f57a37944c07d<SEP>chunk-5d0f74c4239eabf7a6fea87da28be5d8<SEP>chunk-0c3de714c4e42df4c68c8fd79dfac5ad";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "Wounded Child State";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Wounded Child State is a psychological condition formed by childhood emotional wounds, unresolved emotional pain, and inner psychological patterns rooted in past hurts and unhealed trauma. It represents an inner psychological pattern characterized by past pain and inner chaos, which can be relived in present life.

The Wounded Child State influences present behavior, self-perception, and relationships, and can affect career and family dynamics, leading to emotional turmoil, self-destructive behaviors, internal conflict, shame, and self-doubt. It is marked by inner chaos and internal conflict, which may manifest as self-destructive behaviors and negatively impact adult behavior, relationships, and self-perception.

The state can emerge from societal conditioning and emotional suppression, marked by shame, self-doubt, and internal conflict stemming from childhood experiences. It may be addressed through interventions such as the Soul Sync Exercise.

In specific cases, such as Andrew's wounded child state, it can cause significant emotional turmoil, negatively impacting career and family dynamics through self-destructive behaviors.<SEP>The wounded child state represents unresolved past traumas and inner conflict that hinder personal growth, characterized by suffering and self-judgment.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779183826"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source" .

