<urn:mukthiguru:Yesmi> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "The_Four_Sacred_Secrets.pdf<SEP>unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """Yesmi is a monk in a fable who returns to the monastery and approaches a crying woman in need. He helps her cross the river, demonstrating compassion and practicality, embodying monastic virtues of kindness and service. His actions highlight his role as a compassionate figure who intervenes in the lives of those in distress, showing kindness and service.

Yesmi also represents a \"beautiful state\" in the narrative, characterized by inner simplicity, presence, and a connection to the present moment. This state is free from rumination or anxiety and is associated with positive emotional states and constructive actions. He demonstrates a calm, stress-free condition, harmonious actions without causing stress, and is linked to presence and awareness.

In the story, Yesmi's compassion contrasts with Nomi's preoccupation, emphasizing his focus on the present and the needs of others. He exhibits compassion, releases burdens, and demonstrates connection, problem-solving, and compassionate action without self-centered motives.

Yesmi embodies a beautiful state of consciousness, resolving a woman's problem with compassion and presence. He exhibits calmness, presence, compassion, and inner peace, representing a state of presence and non-suffering. His presence is linked to awareness and he is a character who embodies these qualities.<SEP>Yesmi represents a state of presence and awareness associated with resolving distress and fostering connection.` - Correct. A concept.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-cc0f1d606ce37b2df3217415d8473a96<SEP>chunk-2c5321682aea240a40b41c720211188a<SEP>chunk-852cc1672a2a3a688bdf18076d61f76f<SEP>chunk-92e23343f6e8c0c72900c7b35b033bb3<SEP>chunk-7f3bb991411cbbfa162f676b4fd10180<SEP>chunk-184f463e79b52fec37638a498735f009<SEP>chunk-ae33a0629a1035831d09370dbcb6fa05<SEP>chunk-9068ddb93a07ecf743249c1b3afe8709<SEP>chunk-bdc4a608530faeb54a567f51d21bad5a<SEP>chunk-1fc805671f75f5c49fede8b02e05b8db<SEP>chunk-50a3afd25409a52a572d62a449dbc4ec<SEP>chunk-6299fc30fbbfe258eb23a6bd35458a43<SEP>chunk-23f4ae85323a27ae180ceca7fa33c13a<SEP>chunk-bd28b1a048122e44541304a8505b07db<SEP>chunk-1ba7f5be1d21e67ddd5d6d9988215271<SEP>chunk-81f7d5b351616383eb1a7cca9b4d2b48<SEP>chunk-8b68736730809289d016abf18cb33a9d<SEP>chunk-98ebbba09ead01df2486b7e4f58bcc9b";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779183520"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
