<urn:mukthiguru:conscious%20mind> a <neo4j://graph.schema#base>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#source_id> "chunk-61a8f6f1b34dfddc583a21c3b3271137";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> """<think>
Okay, let's tackle this. The user wants me to extract the actual spiritual teaching or concept definition from the contaminated text provided. The contaminated text includes a lot of developer instructions and role descriptions, but I need to focus only on the real content about the \"conscious mind.\"

First, I'll look through the contaminated text. The main part under \"Input\" has the entity name \"conscious mind\" and a list of descriptions. Each description in the list says the same thing: the conscious mind processes 120 bits of information per second and is the smaller, surface layer of mental awareness. There are multiple entries of the same description, which might be redundant, but the key point is that they all repeat the same information.

The task is to synthesize these into a single, comprehensive summary. Since all the descriptions are identical, there's no conflict or variation to reconcile. The entity name is clearly \"conscious mind,\" so I need to start with that. The main points are the 120 bits per second processing and the surface layer aspect. 

I should check if there's any other information, but the contaminated text doesn't add anything else. The developer instructions are about formatting and handling conflicts, but those don't pertain to the actual content. So the clean description should just state that the conscious mind processes 120 bits per second and is the surface layer of awareness. No need for bullet points or headers, just a plain English sentence or two. Since all entries are the same, it's straightforward. No UNPARSEABLE here because there's clear content. Alright, that's it.
</think>

The conscious mind processes approximately 120 bits of information per second, representing the limited capacity of conscious awareness. It functions as the surface layer of mental processing, handling deliberate thoughts and immediate sensory input while underlying cognitive functions operate outside conscious perception. This constrained bandwidth highlights the selective nature of focused attention compared to broader subconscious processing.""";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#created_at> "1779748669"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long>;
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_id> "conscious mind";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#truncate> "";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#file_path> "unknown_source";
  <neo4j://graph.schema#entity_type> "concept" .

