  <neo4j://graph.schema#description> "The Wounded Child represents a state of suffering and self-centric misery, contrasting with the Happy Child's joyful existence.<SEP>Suffering refers to the emotional pain experienced by the daughter, which was alleviated by the spiritual transformation.<SEP>suffering is described as a karmic legacy transmitted through parental consciousness and genes, affecting children's lives." .

